window.CLF_MD = {"m02-03-how-to-provision-aws-resources.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › How to Provision AWS Resources\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-03-how-to-provision-aws-resources-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat is a primary advantage of using the AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI) over the AWS Management Console?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It provides a visual, drag-and-drop interface for managing AWS resources.\n- [ ] B. It is only available for Windows users.\n- [ ] C. It requires fewer configurations and is ideal for one-time manual provisioning.\n- [x] D. It uses automation and scripting, which reduces manual steps and errors.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The AWS CLI enables automation through scripting, which is more efficient and reduces manual errors compared to the console.\n\n<!-- id: m02-03-how-to-provision-aws-resources-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is the customer's responsibility when using compute services like Amazon EC2 according to the AWS shared responsibility model?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS is responsible for managing the operating system, networking, and applications on the customer's EC2 instances.\n- [ ] B. The customer is responsible for securing the physical hardware of their EC2 instances.\n- [ ] C. AWS manages the security of the cloud, and the customer manages the security of the infrastructure.\n- [x] D. The customer is responsible for configuring, securing, and managing the operating system, networking, and applications on their EC2 instances.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The customer handles the operating system, networking, and applications on the EC2 instances. AWS manages the hardware.\n","m07-05-in-memory-caching-services.md":"# Module 7: Databases › In-Memory Caching Services\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m07-05-in-memory-caching-services-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhich problem does Amazon ElastiCache solve?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Performance bottlenecks due to high latency and throughput constraints\n- [ ] B. Cost optimization of infrequently accessed data\n- [ ] C. Network connectivity between on-premises and AWS environments\n- [ ] D. Secure storage of application credentials and secrets\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: ElastiCache addresses performance bottlenecks by caching frequently accessed data in memory, to reduce the load on primary databases and improve response times.\n","m09-05-detecting-and-responding-to-security-incidents.md":"# Module 9: Security › Detecting and Responding to Security Incidents\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m09-05-detecting-and-responding-to-security-incidents-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA security team at a legal firm has detected a threat to their AWS environment. To investigate the root cause over time, they need interactive visualizations of security data. Which AWS service is the BEST choice for this investigation?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Inspector\n- [x] B. Amazon Detective\n- [ ] C. AWS Security Hub\n- [ ] D. Amazon GuardDuty\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Detective is specifically designed for interactive analysis and investigating security threats over time using visualizations. It's a suitable choice for the team's investigation.\n\n<!-- id: m09-05-detecting-and-responding-to-security-incidents-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA local government agency needs to prepare for an upcoming compliance audit. The agency needs to automatically aggregate security findings from multiple AWS services into one comprehensive view. Which of these services should the agency choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Security Hub\n- [ ] B. Amazon Inspector\n- [ ] C. Amazon GuardDuty\n- [ ] D. Amazon Detective\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Security Hub is specifically designed for the aggregation of security findings across multiple AWS services. It's a suitable choice for this use case.\n","m01-07-assessment.md":"# Module 1: Introduction to the Cloud › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou are a software developer working for a company that is planning to migrate its existing application to the cloud. Your team lead has asked you to explain the client-server model to the rest of the team and how cloud computing fits into this model. Which statement BEST describes the client-server model and its relationship to cloud computing?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. In the client-server model, the client sends requests to the server, which processes the requests and sends back responses. Cloud computing provides scalable server resources that can be accessed over the internet.\n- [ ] B. In the client-server model, the server only handles data storage, and the client performs all processing tasks. Cloud computing provides data storage, but not processing power.\n- [ ] C. The client-server model is outdated and no longer used in modern applications. Cloud computing has replaced it completely.\n- [ ] D. In the client-server model, the client is responsible for securing their data, and the server is responsible for securing the physical hardware. Cloud computing replaces the client-server model.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This answer accurately describes the client-server model where the client sends requests to the server. The server processes these requests and returns the appropriate responses. Cloud computing provides scalable and flexible server resources that can be accessed over the internet.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA small business is considering migrating their IT infrastructure to the cloud. The finance team has a meeting with the IT department to discuss the costs associated with this transition. During the meeting, the finance manager says they like the idea of the reliability that comes with the cloud, but they are worried about the fixed costs. Which statement accurately defines the cloud computing model and addresses the finance manager's concern?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Cloud computing involves purchasing dedicated servers and setting up a private data center. This model often comes with fixed costs related to hardware and maintenance.\n- [ ] B. Cloud computing is basically just using someone else's server to host your website, and it does not offer any sort of significant cost advantages over traditional hosting solutions.\n- [ ] C. Cloud computing reduces the need for additional hardware but still involves significant fixed monthly fees.\n- [x] D. Cloud computing is a model for delivering IT resources over the internet. Businesses can rent services on a pay-as-you-go basis, which can help reduce fixed costs and allow for more flexible budgeting.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Cloud computing can be defined as the on-demand delivery of IT resources over the internet with pay-as-you-go pricing. This answer accurately defines cloud computing and directly addresses the finance manager’s concern about fixed costs.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA government agency wants to maintain complete control over its IT infrastructure, but plans to use AWS Cloud services for specific applications. Which deployment type is BEST for this situation?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Cloud\n- [ ] B. Compliance\n- [x] C. Hybrid\n- [ ] D. On-premises\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Hybrid deployment is a solution where the agency can maintain control over on-premises systems while using cloud services for other applications.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA large enterprise is looking to lower operational costs. They are hoping to reduce the operational overhead associated with managing their own physical infrastructure. Which choice BEST describes which advantage of the cloud this enterprise can benefit from?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Increase speed and agility\n- [x] B. Stop spending money running and maintaining data centers\n- [ ] C. Benefit from massive economies of scale\n- [ ] D. Stop guessing capacity\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: By moving to the cloud, the enterprise can offload the responsibility of maintaining physical data centers, reducing operational overhead.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nYou work for a sports apparel company that is expanding its operations to global customers. The company wants to deploy resources to multiple AWS locations to achieve high availability. You are tasked with explaining the basics of AWS Global Infrastructure to your chief operating officer (COO). The COO needs help understanding the difference between AWS Regions and Availability Zones. Which statement BEST describes the difference between AWS Regions and Availability Zones?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. A Region is a single data center, and an Availability Zone consists of multiple data centers.\n- [ ] B. An Availability Zone spans multiple physical locations across Regions, and Regions are located across the world.\n- [x] C. A Region is a geographical location that contains three or more Availability Zones. An Availability Zone is a distinct location within a Region that contains one or more discrete data centers.\n- [ ] D. An Availability Zone is a geographical location that contains three or more Regions. A Region is a distinct location within an Availability Zone that contains one or more discrete data centers.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A Region is a physical location around the world that contains multiple, isolated data centers. An Availability Zone consists of one or more discrete data centers, each with independent power, networking, and connectivity.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nYour company is planning to launch a new web application that will serve users around the world. To help ensure the application performs well and remains reliable, the IT team plans to use AWS for its vast global infrastructure. What BEST describes the benefits of AWS Global Infrastructure related to this situation? (Select TWO.)\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [x] A. High availability\n- [ ] B. Ease of use\n- [ ] C. Cost savings\n- [x] D. Fault tolerance\n- [ ] E. Compliance with regulatory standards\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Global infrastructure typically involves distributing resources across multiple data centers in different geographic locations. By having redundant systems in various locations, global infrastructure enhances fault tolerance. If one component fails, others can take over to minimize downtime and help ensure high availability.Ease of use, compliance, and cost savings are benefits that can be achieved by using cloud resources. However, in this case, the focus is on making resources highly available to global users.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nA finance company is interested in migrating to the cloud. They are curious if they will have enough staff to secure both their office space and the physical infrastructure of their cloud computing resources.Which statement BEST describes the company's responsibility when it comes to securing physical infrastructure of the cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS is responsible for securing the physical infrastructure, and the company can focus on securing their data and applications within the cloud.\n- [ ] B. The company does not have any responsibility when it comes to security in the cloud.\n- [ ] C. The company shares responsibility with the cloud provider for securing the physical infrastructure.\n- [ ] D. The company is fully responsible for securing all physical infrastructure of the cloud, including data centers.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS is responsible for the physical security of data centers. This includes measures like access controls, surveillance, and environmental controls. Companies migrating to the cloud still have responsibilities such as security configurations and data within their cloud environments.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nYou are a cloud architect at a company that has recently migrated its infrastructure to AWS. Your manager has asked you to debrief your team on which responsibilities the customer has when it comes to securing cloud resources. What is the customer's responsibility, based on the AWS Shared Responsibility Model? (Select TWO.)\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [ ] A. Physical security of data centers\n- [x] B. Managing operating system (OS) patches\n- [x] C. Encrypting client-side data\n- [ ] D. Networking and infrastructure hardware maintenance\n- [ ] E. Updating compute, networking, storage, and database software\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: In the AWS Shared Responsibility Model, the customer is responsible for managing OS patches. AWS provides the underlying infrastructure, but the customer must make sure that their OSs are up to date with the latest security patches. The customer is also responsible for encrypting client-side data. AWS provides various services to help with encryption, but it is the customer’s responsibility to implement and manage these services.Physical security of data centers and hardware maintenance are AWS responsibilities. Updating software for compute, networking, storage, and database services is also an AWS responsibility.\n","m06-05-amazon-s3-storage-classes-and-s3-lifecycle.md":"# Module 6: Storage › Amazon S3 Storage Classes and S3 Lifecycle\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m06-05-amazon-s3-storage-classes-and-s3-lifecycle-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAnyCompany Business stores a growing amount of customer data in Amazon S3. Their manager is concerned about storage costs and asks IT to implement a solution to move older data to cheaper storage. The data is frequently accessed for the first 30 days, occasionally accessed for the next 60 days, and rarely accessed after 90 days.What should they do in this situation to optimize costs while maintaining appropriate access to the data?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Create multiple S3 buckets with different storage classes and manually move objects between buckets as they age.\n- [x] B. Create a lifecycle rule to transition objects to S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA) after 30 days, transition to S3 Glacier after 90 days.\n- [ ] C. Create a lifecycle rule to immediately transition all objects to S3 Glacier and set up a restore policy.\n- [ ] D. Create a lifecycle rule to delete all objects after 90 days and rely on database backups.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This policy matches access patterns by using S3 Standard for frequent access, S3 Standard-IA after 30 days of inactivity, and S3 Glacier for archive after 90 days.\n\n<!-- id: m06-05-amazon-s3-storage-classes-and-s3-lifecycle-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhich statement BEST describes S3 Lifecycle?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. A backup service that creates copies of your S3 objects in different AWS Regions to protect against Regional failures.\n- [ ] B. A monitoring system that alerts administrators when Amazon S3 objects have not been accessed for a specified period.\n- [ ] C. A feature that automatically compresses Amazon S3 objects after a certain period to reduce storage costs.\n- [x] D. A feature used to define rules to automatically transition objects between different storage classes, or delete them based on age or usage patterns.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon S3 Lifecycle is used create rules that automate the transition of objects between storage classes. It can set expiration dates for objects based on defined criteria, optimizing storage costs while maintaining access to data based on its changing value over time.\n","m07-02-relational-database-services.md":"# Module 7: Databases › Relational Database Services\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m07-02-relational-database-services-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAnyCompany Retail wants to migrate its product database to the AWS Cloud to reduce operational overhead. Their existing database contains critical inventory and pricing information that requires continuous operation with minimal downtime. Management is exploring Amazon RDS as a way to reduce the number of IT resources. Which feature of Amazon RDS addresses the database requirements described in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Manual snapshot creation\n- [ ] B. Fixed storage allocation\n- [ ] C. Self-managed patching\n- [x] D. Multi-AZ deployments\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Multi-AZ deployments provide enhanced availability and durability by automatically creating database replicas in different Availability Zones. In case of infrastructure failure, Amazon RDS performs an automatic failover to the standby instance, thus ensuring that the database remains accessible with minimal disruption.\n\n<!-- id: m07-02-relational-database-services-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAnyCompany Financial is experiencing slow response times with their current MySQL database during peak transaction periods. It processes over 100,000 transactions per hour and requires high throughput for customer satisfaction. The CTO is looking at Amazon Aurora as a way to significantly improve database performance. Which Aurora feature BEST addresses this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Aurora provides a high-performance, highly available storage architecture that offers up to five times the throughput of standard MySQL.\n- [ ] B. Aurora includes data compression technology that reduces storage requirements for faster query performance.\n- [ ] C. Aurora provides built-in automated instance scaling that adds more CPU resources during peak transaction times.\n- [ ] D. Aurora offers a centralized storage system that eliminates network latency between instances.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The Aurora distributed storage architecture offers up to five times the throughput of standard MySQL while maintaining compatibility. It was specifically designed to handle high transaction workloads by distributing I/O across multiple storage nodes.\n","m06-02-ec2-instance-store-and-amazon-elastic-block-store-amazon-ebs.md":"# Module 6: Storage › EC2 Instance Store and Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS)\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m06-02-ec2-instance-store-and-amazon-elastic-block-store-amazon-ebs-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA developer is building an application that processes large amounts of data and requires high I/O performance. After processing the data for an operation, the results are displayed to the user and do not need to be retained long-term. Unfortunately, the application's current storage solution is experiencing performance bottlenecks during peak processing times. How could implementing an EC2 instance store improve the performance of the application?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. EC2 instance store provides a persistent storage solution that survives instance failures.\n- [ ] B. EC2 instance store allows storage to be conveniently shared between multiple EC2 instances simultaneously.\n- [ ] C. EC2 instance store reduces overall storage costs by offering the cheapest per-gigabyte storage option in AWS.\n- [x] D. EC2 instance store provides high I/O performance for temporary storage needs.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: EC2 instance store is directly attached to the host, offering extremely low latency and high I/O performance for applications that need temporary storage with fast access.\n\n<!-- id: m06-02-ec2-instance-store-and-amazon-elastic-block-store-amazon-ebs-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAnyCompany Finance is designing an application that requires consistent and low-latency access to financial data. They're looking for a storage solution that provides persistent block storage. Why would Amazon EBS be suitable to store data in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon EBS allows sharing volumes across multiple AWS Regions without any latency impact.\n- [ ] B. Amazon EBS automatically scales volume capacity without requiring any volume modifications.\n- [ ] C. Amazon EBS provides unlimited input/output operations per second (IOPS) for all volume types, regardless of size.\n- [x] D. Amazon EBS provides high availability and durability by automatically replicating volumes within the same Availability Zone.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon EBS ensures data protection through automatic replication within the same Availability Zone. This provides the high availability and durability needed for financial applications with critical data.\n\n<!-- id: m06-02-ec2-instance-store-and-amazon-elastic-block-store-amazon-ebs-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nAnyCompany Software is migrating their on-premises application architecture to AWS. They are particularly concerned about data persistence because in their current environment, they have experienced data loss when virtual machines (VMs) crashed. They want to understand how Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) can help address their data persistence requirements when they move their workloads to Amazon EC2 instances. How does Amazon EBS solve the data persistence issue described in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon EBS caches all data in memory for instant recovery when instances are restarted.\n- [ ] B. EBS automatically synchronizes data with Amazon S3 every 5 minutes, ensuring that if an EC2 instance crashes, all data can be immediately restored from the S3 backup.\n- [ ] C. Amazon EBS automatically backs up all data to Amazon S3 every hour to help ensure persistence.\n- [x] D. Amazon EBS volumes exist independently from the instance and persist even after the instance is terminated.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: EBS volumes have a lifecycle that is independent from EC2 instances. They can be detached from one instance and attached to another, and the data remains intact even if the instance is shut down or terminated.\n","m06-12-assessment.md":"# Module 6: Storage › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhich statement BEST describes Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS)?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. An in-memory cache used to improve database performance\n- [ ] B. A temporary storage option that is lost when an instance is stopped or terminated\n- [x] C. A block-level storage service that provides persistent storage volumes for Amazon EC2 instances\n- [ ] D. A file storage system that allows multiple instances to access the same data simultaneously\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon EBS is specifically designed as a block storage service offering persistent volumes that can be attached to EC2 instances and survive instance termination.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAnyCompany Commerce has recently migrated its main application to an Amazon EC2 instance in AWS. As their customer base expands, they are exploring storage solutions that can grow dynamically with the application's data needs.The solution needs to meet the following criteria: Have persistent block storage that provides consistent low-latency performance.Be able to be attached to and detached from the EC2 instance as needed.Independently resize storage capacity without disrupting the instance.Create point-in-time backups to protect critical customer and inventory data.Which AWS storage service would BEST meet the requirements in the scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS)\n- [ ] B. Amazon FSx\n- [ ] C. Amazon S3\n- [ ] D. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon EBS provides persistent block storage volumes that can be attached to EC2 instances. It offers consistent low-latency performance, can be scaled independently of the EC2 instance, and supports point-in-time snapshots for backup purposes.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nAnyCompany AI is developing a machine learning application that requires extremely fast data processing for temporary model training datasets. The data is generated during training sessions and stored separately in persistent storage. The team is trying to determine the best storage solution to use alongside their application.The solution needs to meet the following criteria: Highest possible I/O performanceDirectly attached to their Amazon EC2 instancesTemporary storage – data does not persist when instances are stopped or terminatedWhich AWS service BEST meets the temporary storage needs described in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon EC2 instance store\n- [ ] B. Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS)\n- [ ] C. Amazon S3\n- [ ] D. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: EC2 instance store provides temporary block-level storage that is physically attached to the host computer, offering the highest possible I/O performance for temporary data processing needs.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nAnyCompany Software is deploying a critical production application on Amazon EC2 instances with several Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes containing application code and customer data. The team is looking for an AWS service they can use to back up the data for their application.The solution needs to meet the following criteria:Create regular data backups.Create duplicate environments for testing.Create a disaster recovery strategy.Create full or incremental backups without impacting application performance.Provide cost-effective for long-term storage.Which AWS service or feature would BEST meet the requirements in the scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. EBS snapshots\n- [ ] B. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\n- [ ] C. Amazon S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval\n- [ ] D. Amazon FSx\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: EBS snapshots are point-in-time copies of EBS volumes that can be used for regular backups, creating duplicate volumes for testing, and enabling fast disaster recovery by restoring entire volumes from snapshots.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nWhich statement BEST describes Amazon S3?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. A scalable object storage service that is used to store and retrieve any amount of data from anywhere on the web.\n- [ ] B. A storage service primarily designed for long-term archival and backup of data that is rarely accessed.\n- [ ] C. A file storage service that provides a traditional file system interface for sharing files between multiple instances.\n- [ ] D. A block-level storage service that provides persistent storage for Amazon EC2 instances.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon S3 is fundamentally an object storage service designed for scalability. Users can store unlimited amounts of data that can be accessed from anywhere with internet connectivity.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nAnyCompany Marketing needs a storage solution that they can use to distribute large collections of high-resolution images, videos, and design files for their clients' campaigns. Some assets are accessed frequently, whereas others are archived for occasional reference.The solution needs to meet the following criteria:Unlimited storage capacityHigh durabilityEasy file sharing through URLsAbility to organize assets by client and projectCost-efficient storage optionsSecurity controls to prevent unauthorized access for specific assetsWhich AWS service is BEST suited for the storage needs described in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon S3\n- [ ] B. Amazon FSx\n- [ ] C. Amazon Elastic Block Storage (Amazon EBS)\n- [ ] D. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon S3 provides scalable object storage ideal for storing and distributing media files. It includes features like lifecycle policies for cost optimization, bucket organization for client projects, access controls for security, and the ability to generate URLs for easy file sharing.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nWhat is the primary function of Amazon S3 storage classes?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. To replicate data across multiple AWS Regions automatically\n- [x] B. To provide different storage options optimized for different use cases and access patterns\n- [ ] C. To encrypt data at rest and in transit\n- [ ] D. To organize objects within buckets hierarchically\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon S3 storage classes are designed to offer different performance characteristics, availability levels, and cost structures to match specific data storage requirements and access patterns.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nWhat is a key characteristic of Amazon S3 storage classes pricing?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Pricing varies based on storage costs, retrieval fees, and minimum storage durations.\n- [ ] B. All storage classes cost the same but differ in retrieval speed.\n- [ ] C. Pricing is exclusively determined by the geographic region of the bucket.\n- [ ] D. All storage classes have the same minimum storage duration requirement.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon S3 storage classes have different pricing structures that affect the overall cost. These include storage costs per gigabyte, potential data retrieval charges, and minimum storage duration commitments.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q9 -->\n## Question 9\n\nWhich statement BEST describes Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. An object storage service designed for long-term archival of rarely accessed data\n- [ ] B. A fixed-capacity file storage system that requires manual scaling and management\n- [ ] C. A block storage service that provides volumes to attach to single Amazon EC2 instance\n- [x] D. A fully managed, elastic file system that scales automatically as files are added and removed\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This accurately describes the Amazon EFS core value proposition as a service that automatically grows and shrinks with the storage needs without manual provisioning.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q10 -->\n## Question 10\n\nAnyCompany Technology needs to implement a centralized storage solution for their development team that allows multiple Amazon EC2 instances to access the same file system simultaneously.The solution needs to meet the following criteria:Provide a fully managed service.Automatically scale.Eliminate the need for capacity planning.Support Linux-based applications with standard file system interfaces.Maintain consistent low-latency access across development environments.Provide high durability without requiring complex replication setups.Which AWS storage service is BEST suited for this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Elastic Block Storage (Amazon EBS)\n- [x] B. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\n- [ ] C. Amazon S3\n- [ ] D. Amazon FSx\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon EFS provides a scalable, fully managed elastic network file system (NFS) that can be accessed concurrently by multiple EC2 instances. It automatically grows as data is added and offers POSIX compliance for Linux applications.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q11 -->\n## Question 11\n\nWhich statement BEST describes Amazon FSx?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. An object storage solution designed for archiving rarely accessed data\n- [x] B. A fully managed service that provides cost-effective, scalable file storage built on widely used file systems\n- [ ] C. A block storage service that provides high performance volumes for EC2 instances\n- [ ] D. A service used to set up private file sharing within an on-premises data center only\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon FSx is specifically designed as a fully managed service that offers file storage based on popular file systems like Windows File Server, Lustre, OpenZFS, and NetApp ONTAP.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q12 -->\n## Question 12\n\nAnyCompany Marketing needs to migrate their existing file shares to AWS to support their design teams who work with large creative files. They need help choosing a storage solution that can facilitate this migration.The solution needs to meet the following requirements:Provide a fully managed service.Seamlessly integrate with Windows applications.Support SMB protocol.Offer Active Directory integration for user authentication.Support data deduplication to optimize storage costs.Provide consistent sub-millisecond latencies.Provide high availability.Which AWS storage service BEST meets the requirements described in the scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\n- [x] B. Amazon FSx for Windows File Server\n- [ ] C. Amazon Storage Gateway\n- [ ] D. Amazon S3\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon FSx for Windows File Server is specifically designed for Windows workloads. It provides SMB support, Active Directory integration, and Windows features like data deduplication, while delivering consistent sub-millisecond latencies as a fully managed service.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q13 -->\n## Question 13\n\nWhich statement BEST describes AWS Storage Gateway?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. A migration tool that automatically transfers all on-premises data to the cloud\n- [ ] B. A physical hardware appliance that must be installed in a data center\n- [ ] C. A virtual private network that creates secure connections between a data center and AWS\n- [x] D. A hybrid cloud storage solution that provides on-premises applications with access to virtually unlimited cloud storage\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Storage Gateway is fundamentally designed as a hybrid solution that connects on-premises environments to AWS Cloud storage. This allows local applications to seamlessly access AWS storage while maintaining local access patterns.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q14 -->\n## Question 14\n\nWhich statement BEST describes AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. A backup service that creates periodic snapshots of AWS resources and stores them in Amazon S3 buckets\n- [ ] B. A managed database service that provides automated backups and cross-Region replication\n- [ ] C. A service that automatically scales computing capacity based on workload demands during disaster events\n- [x] D. A service that minimizes downtime and data loss by providing fast, reliable recovery of on-premises and cloud-based applications using affordable storage, minimal compute, and point-in-time recovery\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This accurately describes the core functionality of Elastic Disaster Recovery, which focuses on continuous replication to help provide rapid recovery with minimal data loss.\n\n<!-- id: m06-12-assessment-q15 -->\n## Question 15\n\nAnyCompany Manufacturing maintains a large amount of engineering drawings and design files that their teams need to access daily from their on-premises applications. They want to gradually migrate these files to AWS to reduce their local storage costs while maintaining low-latency access for frequently used files.The solution needs to meet the following criteria:Integrate with existing file-based workflows.Provide a seamless path to cloud storage without disrupting current operations.Maintain local, low-latency access to frequently used files.Which AWS storage service should they use based on these requirements?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Storage Gateway – File Gateway\n- [ ] B. Amazon S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval\n- [ ] C. Amazon FSx for Windows File Server\n- [ ] D. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: File Gateway provides a file interface into Amazon S3 object storage. It maintains low-latency local access to frequently accessed data through local caching and seamlessly integrates with existing file-based workflows.\n","m06-04-amazon-simple-storage-service-amazon-s3.md":"# Module 6: Storage › Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3)\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m06-04-amazon-simple-storage-service-amazon-s3-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAnyCompany Mobile is evaluating cloud storage solutions for their new mobile application. They need a reliable service that can handle various types of data storage requirements as their user base grows.Based on this scenario, what is an aspect of Amazon S3 that they could use in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Running relational database queries for user authentication\n- [ ] B. Real-time data streaming and message processing\n- [x] C. Storing and distributing mobile application content and user-generated media files\n- [ ] D. Hosting virtual machines (VMs) to process application logic\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon S3 is designed for scalable object storage that can efficiently store and serve various content types. It's ideal for mobile applications that need to store and distribute user-generated content like photos and videos.\n\n<!-- id: m06-04-amazon-simple-storage-service-amazon-s3-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAnyCompany Marketing has created an Amazon S3 bucket to host images for their new website. The images need to be accessible to anyone visiting the website without authentication. After uploading the images to the bucket, users report they cannot access them, even though the bucket policy is set to allow public access.What is the most likely cause of this access issue?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Block public access settings are enabled at the account or bucket level.\n- [ ] B. The S3 bucket must be in the same AWS Region as the users trying to access the content.\n- [ ] C. The images are not properly tagged with public read permissions.\n- [ ] D. They need to enable the website hosting feature to make any Amazon S3 content public.\n\n> Correct! Rationale: S3 Block Public Access settings override bucket policies, preventing public access even when policies allow it.\n\n<!-- id: m06-04-amazon-simple-storage-service-amazon-s3-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nAnyCompany Media is looking for a new cloud storage solution. They distribute large video files to users around the world, and are looking for a service that is highly durable, scalable, and offers various access control mechanisms.Based on this scenario, which Amazon S3 feature would be particularly beneficial?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon S3 limits individual object sizes to 5 GB, requiring companies to split large video files before upload.\n- [ ] B. Amazon S3 provides built-in video transcoding services that automatically convert videos to different formats when they are uploaded.\n- [x] C. Amazon S3 offers 99.999999999 percent (11 nines) of durability for objects stored across multiple Availability Zones. This maintains highly available for their video content and protects it against data loss.\n- [ ] D. Amazon S3 automatically compresses all stored objects to reduce storage costs by up to 90 percent, making it ideal for large video files.\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon S3 is designed with this durability level as a key feature, which is critical for valuable media assets that cannot be conveniently recreated if lost.\n","m10-04-aws-cloudtrail.md":"# Module 10: Monitoring, Compliance, and Governance in the AWS Cloud › AWS CloudTrail\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m10-04-aws-cloudtrail-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA company wants to store the files that contain API activities for an AWS account in an Amazon S3 bucket. They want to retain these files for auditing and compliance.Which solution and feature would provide this capability?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS CloudTrail logs\n- [ ] B. Amazon CloudWatch Logs\n- [ ] C. AWS CloudTrail events\n- [ ] D. AWS CloudTrail Insights\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: CloudTrail logs can be delivered to an S3 bucket or Amazon CloudWatch logs and are not limited to 90 days.\n","m11-07-assessment.md":"# Module 11: Pricing and Support › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m11-07-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA global finance company currently has their information technology (IT) resources on-premises and is evaluating the AWS Cloud. The company is used to fixed capital expenditures and wants to understand how they would pay by moving to the AWS Cloud. Which choices BEST describe how customers pay for AWS?\n\n_Choose 3_\n\n- [ ] A. Save by using fixed expenses\n- [x] B. Pay as you go\n- [ ] C. Sign fixed contracts\n- [x] D. Pay less by using more\n- [x] E. Save when you commit\n- [ ] F. Pay all upfront\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: When it comes to AWS pricing, customers pay as they go and can save when they commit to a specific amount of usage for a certain period of time. They can also get volume-based discounts as their usage increases.\n\n<!-- id: m11-07-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAn EdTech company is considering moving their education application to the cloud. The company's chief financial officer (CFO) wants to understand how AWS services are priced and which factors will drive their cost. Although pricing varies based on several factors, which options are the fundamental drivers of cost with AWS?\n\n_Choose 3_\n\n- [x] A. Compute\n- [ ] B. Support\n- [x] C. Storage\n- [x] D. Outbound data transfer\n- [ ] E. Inbound data transfer\n- [ ] F. Security\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The cost of an AWS service or category of services can be impacted by several factors. However, the primary driving factors of cost are compute, storage, and outbound data transfer.\n\n<!-- id: m11-07-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nYou are part of a team that wants to monitor and manage costs of multiple AWS accounts across different departments within your organization. Which AWS service can you use to effectively manage and consolidate billing information for these accounts?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Cost Explorer\n- [ ] B. AWS Billing and Cost Management dashboard\n- [ ] C. AWS Budgets\n- [x] D. AWS Organizations\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Organizations is designed to help you manage multiple AWS accounts, including consolidating billing information, setting up policies, and enforcing governance across your organization.\n\n<!-- id: m11-07-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nAn online retail company is interested in moving forward with the migration of an application, but they would like to estimate costs before diving in. Which tool or service can they use to estimate the cost of the specific AWS services and configurations that they need?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Cost Explorer is a tool that the company can use to view and analyze their costs and usage.\n- [x] B. AWS Pricing Calculator is a web-based tool that the company can use to configure cost estimates for their unique business needs.\n- [ ] C. AWS Organizations is a service that the company can use to centrally manage and govern their environment as they grow and scale their AWS resources.\n- [ ] D. With AWS Budgets, the company can monitor their aggregate utilization and coverage metrics.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Pricing Calculator is the right tool to suggest for configuring cost estimates based on unique customer needs.\n\n<!-- id: m11-07-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nYou are the chief technology officer of a large enterprise with mission-critical applications running on AWS. Your organization requires the highest level of support, including response times of 15 minutes or less when mission-critical systems are down. Which AWS support plan should you choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Business Support\n- [x] B. Enterprise Support\n- [ ] C. Developer Support\n- [ ] D. Basic Support\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Enterprise Support is designed for large enterprises with mission-critical applications. It offers the highest level of support, including rapid response times, proactive monitoring, and access to a wide range of AWS services and features. Additionally, it provides guidance from AWS experts to help ensure optimal performance and security.\n\n<!-- id: m11-07-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nYou are the technical lead for a mid-sized e-commerce company and are evaluating various support options for your AWS infrastructure. Your current challenges include optimizing database performance and incident response planning. You are also seeking technical consulting on best practices for security. Outside of standard AWS Support Plans, which support option is the BEST choice for getting advice on best practices for security and for conducting a security audit of your AWS environment?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Professional Services\n- [ ] B. AWS re:Post\n- [ ] C. AWS Trust and Safety Team\n- [ ] D. AWS Basic Support\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Professional Services offers deep technical expertise and can assist with security audits, best practices, and strategic guidance tailored to specific needs.\n\n<!-- id: m11-07-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nIn addition to AWS Support Plans and other technical assistance options, AWS also provides access to self-support resources. Which options do AWS customers have available as self-support resources?\n\n_Choose 3_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Documentation, such as user guides for AWS services\n- [x] B. SDK guides\n- [ ] C. AWS Professional Services\n- [x] D. AWS Blog\n- [ ] E. AWS solutions architects\n- [ ] F. AWS Trust and Safety Center\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: These are all types of resources available to AWS customers looking to find a cloud solution through self-support.\n\n<!-- id: m11-07-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nA large enterprise wants to find compliance-ready software solutions to make sure they meet industry regulations. They are exploring AWS services to help with this, and they want to implement the solution as quickly as possible.What option is the BEST fit for this enterprise and their requirements?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Use AWS Shield to protect against distributed denial of service (DDoS) attacks.\n- [ ] B. Develop custom solutions in-house.\n- [ ] C. Use self-support tools such as AWS Documentation.\n- [x] D. Find compliance-ready solutions in the AWS Marketplace.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Marketplace offers a variety of software solutions such as compliance-ready software. This enterprise can use the AWS Marketplace to quickly find and implement a solution that meets their specific needs.\n\n<!-- id: m11-07-assessment-q9 -->\n## Question 9\n\nWhich option BEST describes the role of the AWS Partner Network (APN)?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Offering certification for AWS users\n- [ ] B. Providing customer support for AWS users\n- [ ] C. Developing new AWS services and features\n- [x] D. Helping businesses build, market, and sell solutions based in AWS\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The APN helps AWS Partners build, market, and sell solutions based in AWS by providing them with technical, marketing, and go-to-market support.\n\n<!-- id: m11-07-assessment-q10 -->\n## Question 10\n\nWhich option BEST describes a key benefit of being an AWS Partner?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Early access to all AWS services\n- [ ] B. Dedicated AWS hardware\n- [x] C. AWS Partner Funding benefits\n- [ ] D. Exclusive access to all AWS Training and Certification\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: One of the key benefits of being an AWS Partner is access to various funding benefits. These can include financial incentives, marketing support, and go-to-market funding that help partners build, market, and sell their solutions on AWS.\n","m08-01-introduction-to-ai-and-machine-learning.md":"# Module 8: AI/ML and Data Analytics › Introduction to AI and Machine Learning\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m08-01-introduction-to-ai-and-machine-learning-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nMachine learning (ML) is a type of AI for training machines to perform complex tasks without explicit instructions. This training process involves finding patterns in vast amounts of historical data. What is produced as a result of the ML training process?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. An ML database cataloging the types of data found\n- [ ] B. An explicit ML rule book that dictates how to perform tasks\n- [x] C. An ML model that can make predictions or decisions\n- [ ] D. An ML data report that summarizes the data\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: ML training produces a model that can be applied to new data to make predictions or decisions based on the patterns it is learned.\n","m02-08-messaging-and-queuing.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Messaging and Queuing\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-08-messaging-and-queuing-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat BEST describes the key difference between tightly coupled and loosely coupled architectures?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. In a tightly coupled architecture, components are tightly connected and dependent on each other, whereas in a loosely coupled architecture, components can operate independently.\n- [ ] B. Tightly coupled architectures are designed for scalability, whereas loosely coupled systems focus on maintaining high availability.\n- [ ] C. Loosely coupled systems require components to share data directly with each other, whereas tightly coupled systems store data in a central repository.\n- [ ] D. Tightly coupled systems are more flexible in adding new components, whereas loosely coupled systems require careful configuration to add new components.\n\n> Correct! Rationale: In tightly coupled systems, components are heavily interdependent. If one component fails, it can cause cascading failures. In contrast, loosely coupled systems have components that operate independently, so the failure of one component does not disrupt the entire system.\n\n<!-- id: m02-08-messaging-and-queuing-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nIn a banking system, when customers transfer money, the transaction details are sent from the transaction service to a fraud detection service for verification. Sometimes, the fraud detection service is temporarily down.What is the MAIN advantage of using Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) in this banking scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It speeds up transaction processing by avoiding the use of a buffer.\n- [x] B. It stores transaction details until the fraud detection service can process them, even if the service is down.\n- [ ] C. It guarantees immediate approval of transactions.\n- [ ] D. It forces the transaction service and fraud detection service to depend on each other directly.\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon SQS safely stores transaction details until the fraud detection service can process them, preventing data loss when the service is unavailable.\n","m05-03-more-ways-to-connect-to-the-aws-cloud.md":"# Module 5: Networking › More Ways to Connect to the AWS Cloud\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-03-more-ways-to-connect-to-the-aws-cloud-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA company is conducting a large-scale migration of their on-premises data center with their data warehouse and data backup. They need a solution that will meet the large amount of bandwidth requirements during migration. The solution will also be used for their ongoing data transfers after the move because they will retain part of their on-premises data center for a hybrid cloud solution.Which AWS solution would best meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Direct Connect link to their on-premises network and the AWS Cloud\n- [ ] B. AWS Site-to-Site VPN\n- [ ] C. AWS Client VPN\n- [ ] D. AWS Private Link to their on-premises datacenter\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Direct Connect would provide the bandwidth requirements for the migration, in addition to the ongoing data transfers in their hybrid solution.\n\n<!-- id: m05-03-more-ways-to-connect-to-the-aws-cloud-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA company is choosing the type of gateway for their network. They need to connect their corporate data center with their private subnet in their Amazon Virtual Private Cloud. Their gateway needs to allow only protected internet traffic to enter into the Amazon VPC. It should also allow a connection between their Amazon VPC and a private network only if it is coming from an approved network.Which type of gateway would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Virtual private gateway\n- [ ] B. Amazon API Gateway\n- [ ] C. AWS Transit Gateway\n- [ ] D. Internet gateway\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A virtual private gateway is the component that allows protected internet traffic to enter into the VPC. This is perfect because it will restrict access to only protected internet traffic.\n","m05-06-global-networking.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Global Networking\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-06-global-networking-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAn enterprise customer with a worldwide sales force is looking to deliver their large library of sales training content. They want to make sure their sales force can access the media-rich training content with low latency and reduced costs.Which AWS service would BEST fit the customer's need?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon CloudFront\n- [ ] B. AWS Global Accelerator\n- [ ] C. Amazon Route 53\n- [ ] D. Amazon VPC\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: CloudFront is a service that uses the AWS global network to improve application availability, performance, and security.\n\n<!-- id: m05-06-global-networking-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAfter years of working with different domain registration companies, a media company is looking for a solution to manage all their existing domain names. They also want to register new domain names. Ideally, they would like to manage all their domain names in a single service.Which AWS service would BEST fit the customer's need?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon VPC\n- [x] B. Amazon Route 53\n- [ ] C. Amazon CloudFront\n- [ ] D. AWS Global Accelerator\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Route 53 is a highly available and scalable cloud DNS service. It will makes it possible for the customer to manage all their domains in a single service.\n","m10-07-aws-organizations.md":"# Module 10: Monitoring, Compliance, and Governance in the AWS Cloud › AWS Organizations\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m10-07-aws-organizations-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou are configuring service control policies (SCPs) in AWS Organizations. Which identities and resources can SCPs be applied to? (Select TWO.)\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) users\n- [ ] B. AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) groups\n- [x] C. An individual member account\n- [ ] D. AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) roles\n- [x] E. An organizational unit (OU)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A service that uses the AWS global network to improve application availability, performance, and security.\n","m11-03-aws-pricing-and-billing-services.md":"# Module 11: Pricing and Support › AWS Pricing and Billing Services\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m11-03-aws-pricing-and-billing-services-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA government agency is getting started with managing their AWS Cloud costs. They want to set up notifications to alert them when costs exceed a certain threshold for any given month. Which AWS service would they use to achieve this task?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Budgets\n- [ ] B. AWS Pricing Calculator\n- [ ] C. AWS Cost Explorer\n- [ ] D. AWS Organizations\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Budgets helps customers set custom budgets and receive notifications when their costs or usage exceed defined thresholds, making it ideal for this scenario.\n","m09-03-protecting-networks-and-applications.md":"# Module 9: Security › Protecting Networks and Applications\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m09-03-protecting-networks-and-applications-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nIn a denial of service (DoS) attack, an attacker floods a web application with excessive network traffic. Legitimate customer requests are denied if the web application becomes overloaded and can no longer respond. How is a distributed denial of service (DDoS) attack different?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. A DDoS attack distributes malware to end users instead of overwhelming network resources.\n- [ ] B. A DDoS attack targets multiple websites simultaneously instead of focusing on a single target.\n- [x] C. A DDoS attack uses multiple compromised computers and devices to launch the attack.\n- [ ] D. A DDoS attack distributes the incoming traffic across multiple servers to prevent service interruption.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Unlike a regular DoS attack from a single source, DDoS attacks use networks of compromised computers to send traffic to the target.\n\n<!-- id: m09-03-protecting-networks-and-applications-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAn online boutique has recently suffered a series of targeted distributed denial of service (DDoS) attacks. The owner wants to enhance the security of the boutique's web application using AWS infrastructure. Which components can the boutique use to protect the web application on AWS from DDoS attacks?\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [ ] A. Auto scaling groups\n- [x] B. Security groups\n- [ ] C. Compute instances\n- [ ] D. Public subnets\n- [x] E. Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Security groups make sure only traffic from authenticated users is allowed into the system, while an ELB distributes incoming traffic to prevent any single frontend server from being overwhelmed. Operating at the AWS network level, these components leverage the full capacity of the AWS Region to help absorb large-scale attacks.\n","m01-02-what-is-cloud-computing.md":"# Module 1: Introduction to the Cloud › What is Cloud Computing?\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m01-02-what-is-cloud-computing-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou work for a local charity organization. Your organization has sensitive data that must remain within your country for compliance reasons. However, you also need a solution that can scale quickly to handle seasonal spikes in demand. You decide to keep on-premises resources for compliance and use cloud-based resources for dynamic scaling. Which type of cloud deployment does this situation describe?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. On-premises deployment\n- [ ] B. Public cloud deployment\n- [x] C. Hybrid deployment\n- [ ] D. Data-compliance deployment\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With a hybrid cloud solution, you can keep sensitive data on-premises to meet compliance requirements while using cloud-based resources for dynamic scaling.\n","m09-01-introduction-to-security-on-aws.md":"# Module 9: Security › Introduction to Security on AWS\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m09-01-introduction-to-security-on-aws-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAfter logging in to their online banking profile with their username and password, a customer attempts to transfer $10,000 from their savings to their checking account. The system checks if the customer has sufficient privileges to make transfers of this amount before proceeding. Which type of system check is this an example of?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Authorization\n- [ ] B. Auditing\n- [ ] C. Encryption\n- [ ] D. Authentication\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: In this scenario, the system is checking if the customer has the right to transfer $10,000, which is an authorization control. The system verifies their privileges (what they are allowed to do).\n\n<!-- id: m09-01-introduction-to-security-on-aws-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA healthcare company is preparing to deploy a web application on Amazon EC2 instances that will process sensitive patient data. The application will use Amazon RDS for database storage and Amazon S3 for file storage. The company's security team is discussing security responsibilities for the deployment. What is the customer's security responsibility in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Protecting sensitive patient data stored in Amazon S3 and Amazon RDS\n- [ ] B. Replacing faulty hardware components that might affect EC2 instance availability\n- [ ] C. Protecting the physical security of the data centers where the EC2 instances are hosted\n- [ ] D. Maintaining and patching the underlying hypervisor infrastructure for Amazon EC2\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Under the AWS shared responsibility model, customers are responsible for protecting their sensitive data stored in AWS services like Amazon S3 and Amazon RDS.\n","m06-08-amazon-fsx.md":"# Module 6: Storage › Amazon FSx\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m06-08-amazon-fsx-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAnyCompany Media wants to migrate its file shares to AWS while maintaining compatibility with existing applications. They need a solution that supports Server Message Block (SMB) protocol and integrates with Microsoft Active Directory.Which AWS service should they implement in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS)\n- [ ] B. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\n- [ ] C. Amazon S3 File Gateway\n- [x] D. Amazon FSx for Windows File Server\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: FSx for Windows File Server is a fully managed Windows file system. It supports SMB protocol, integrates with Active Directory, and provides the Windows compatibility needed for this scenario.\n","m07-03-nosql-database-services.md":"# Module 7: Databases › NoSQL Database Services\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m07-03-nosql-database-services-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA staffing resource company is building an application that must store employee information with unpredictable traffic patterns. Their application requires consistent performance at all times, and the development team wants to focus on features rather than database management tasks.Which Amazon DynamoDB capability BEST addresses the needs for this workload?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Auto scaling with provisioned capacity\n- [ ] B. Predefined schema enforcement\n- [ ] C. Manual configuration of read/write capacity units\n- [ ] D. Fixed storage limit allocation\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Auto scaling with provisioned capacity means that DynamoDB can automatically adjust capacity in response to actual traffic patterns. This keeps application performance consistent during unpredictable peaks in traffic, while optimizing costs during slower periods.\n","m01-03-benefits-of-the-aws-cloud.md":"# Module 1: Introduction to the Cloud › Benefits of the AWS Cloud\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m01-03-benefits-of-the-aws-cloud-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA retail business plans to launch a new line of clothing, but they are struggling with accurately predicting how much server capacity they will need to support the launch.Which benefit of the AWS Cloud is most relevant to this situation?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Stop spending money to run and maintain data centers.\n- [x] B. Stop guessing capacity.\n- [ ] C. Trade upfront expense for variable expense.\n- [ ] D. Go global in minutes.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With the AWS Cloud, the company can conveniently scale resources up or down based on actual demand, eliminating the need to guess future capacity requirements.\n","m02-07-directing-traffic-with-elastic-load-balancing.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Directing Traffic with Elastic Load Balancing\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-07-directing-traffic-with-elastic-load-balancing-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nHow does Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) improve scalability in AWS?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It manually adjusts the number of Amazon EC2 instances based on traffic.\n- [x] B. It automatically routes traffic to instances based on various routing methods.\n- [ ] C. It directly increases the size of Amazon EC2 instances.\n- [ ] D. It creates new Amazon EC2 instances for each request.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: ELB improves scalability by automatically distributing traffic to the EC2 instances with the least load, resulting in efficient traffic management. ELB scales elastically. This means it adjusts traffic routing based on demand without increasing hourly costs, which is a key benefit.\n\n<!-- id: m02-07-directing-traffic-with-elastic-load-balancing-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhich task does Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) perform?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Distributes a workload across several Amazon EC2 instances.\n- [ ] B. Removes unneeded Amazon EC2 instances when demand is low.\n- [ ] C. Adds a second Amazon EC2 instance during an online store's popular sale.\n- [ ] D. Automatically adjusts the number of Amazon EC2 instances to match demand.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: ELB and Auto Scaling work together to efficiently manage varying levels of demand. ELB is responsible for distributing incoming traffic evenly across multiple EC2 instances. This makes sure that no single instance becomes overwhelmed. It also serves as a single-entry point for traffic into an Auto Scaling group, directing requests to the appropriate resources.Meanwhile, Auto Scaling automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances based on the demand. It adds or removes instances as needed for optimal performance and resource usage. Together, ELB and Auto Scaling help maintain application reliability and cost efficiency.\n","m03-05-assessment.md":"# Module 3: Exploring Compute Services › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat is the customer responsible for managing in a serverless service like AWS Lambda?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The physical servers and networking hardware\n- [ ] B. The operating system, network configuration, and application stack\n- [ ] C. Nothing—AWS manages everything\n- [x] D. The application code\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With serverless services like Lambda, customers are responsible for the application code. AWS manages the infrastructure, scaling, and availability.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA developer is launching a new microservice and wants to focus only on writing and deploying code. They do not want to manage servers, handle scaling, or worry about infrastructure availability. Which AWS service model is BEST for this use case?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Unmanaged\n- [ ] B. On premises\n- [x] C. Serverless\n- [ ] D. Hybrid cloud\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With serverless services, customers can focus solely on writing and deploying code. AWS fully manages infrastructure, scaling, and availability, so customers do not have to worry about managing servers or capacity.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nWhich scenario is the BEST fit for using AWS Lambda?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Automatically processing images as users upload them to an Amazon S3 bucket\n- [ ] B. Running a relational database that needs complex queries and frequent connections\n- [ ] C. Hosting a high-traffic web server that requires full control over the operating system (OS)\n- [ ] D. Running a large, high-performance computing workload that takes several hours to complete\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Lambda is perfect for this event-driven use case. It can run code in response to uploads and scale automatically based on the number of events.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA company is launching a containerized photo application and has built the container image, which needs to be stored securely. They plan to use Kubernetes for orchestration and prefer not to manage any servers. Which combination of AWS services BEST fits their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon S3, Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), and Amazon EC2\n- [x] B. Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR), Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS), and AWS Fargate\n- [ ] C. Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR), AWS Lambda, and Amazon EC2\n- [ ] D. Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR), Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), and Amazon EC2\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon ECR stores container images, Amazon EKS handles Kubernetes orchestration, and AWS Fargate runs containers without server management. This combination offers seamless orchestration with no infrastructure maintenance.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nA development team at a travel company has stored their hotel booking system’s container image in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) and is ready to deploy it. They need a service that can automatically start and stop containers based on traffic, scale up or down with demand, and monitor the health of the system. Which service does the team need next?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon EC2 with auto scaling\n- [x] B. An orchestration service like Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) or Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS)\n- [ ] C. A virtual machine to run the container manually\n- [ ] D. AWS Lambda\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon ECS or Amazon EKS can automatically scale containers, handle health checks, and manage their lifecycle based on traffic demand, which fits the team’s requirements.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nA development team at an e-commerce company is working on a new website. The application runs fine on their local machines, but when they attempt to deploy it to a staging environment, it does not work as expected. The team wants to make sure that the application runs consistently across all development, testing, and production environments going forward. Which solution should the team use to make sure that the application runs the same across all environments?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Set up separate environments for each operating system.\n- [ ] B. Use different versions of the applications for different environments.\n- [ ] C. Use Amazon EC2 to manually recreate the development environment.\n- [x] D. Package the application in a container that includes all dependencies.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Containers bundle the application, runtime, and dependencies together, providing consistency across all environments from development to production.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nA pharmaceutical research company needs to run thousands of simulations to analyze protein folding. These compute-heavy tasks are run in parallel and do not require real-time interaction. The company wants the jobs to be automatically scheduled and scaled based on computing demand. Which AWS service BEST fits this workload?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Batch\n- [ ] B. Amazon Lightsail\n- [ ] C. AWS Elastic Beanstalk\n- [ ] D. AWS Lambda\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Batch is designed for large-scale batch workloads and can automatically manage and scale compute resources for job queues.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nA freelance developer is building a blog for a client with minimal traffic. They want a basic, cost-effective solution that includes storage and compute in one package, without having to deal with complex configurations or scaling concerns. Which AWS service is the BEST fit?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Fargate\n- [x] B. Amazon Lightsail\n- [ ] C. AWS Batch\n- [ ] D. AWS Lambda\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Lightsail is great for small projects like blogs and basic websites, and it offers predictable pricing and ease of use.\n","m05-07-global-architectures.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Global Architectures\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-07-global-architectures-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA healthcare company is looking to create a dedicated network connection to AWS. They would use this connection for their heavy payloads of data being sent over the internet to AWS. They also have compliance requirements due to the sensitive nature of their patient data.Which type of connection to the AWS Cloud would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. VPN connection from their corporate data center to the AWS Cloud\n- [x] B. AWS Direct Connect connection from their corporate data center to a virtual private gateway in their VPC in the AWS Cloud\n- [ ] C. Standard internet connection from the client to an internet gateway in the VPC in the AWS Cloud\n- [ ] D. VPN connection from their corporate data center to a virtual private gateway to their Amazon VPC\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Direct Connect connection would provide both the bandwidth for the large data payloads and the security requirements needed for compliance.\n","m12-04-migration-services-and-tools.md":"# Module 12: Migrating to the AWS Cloud › Migration Services and Tools\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m12-04-migration-services-and-tools-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA customer is getting started on their migration and is not sure how to build a business case to justify their move.Which solution would BEST meet the requirements?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Migration Evaluator\n- [ ] B. AWS Application Discovery Service\n- [ ] C. AWS Application Migration Service\n- [ ] D. AWS Migration Hub\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Migration Evaluator is a migration assessment service that helps create a business case for AWS Cloud planning and migration.\n\n<!-- id: m12-04-migration-services-and-tools-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA customer is looking for a tool to help centralize the view of all their migration tasks and help track their migration.Which solution would BEST meet the requirements?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Application Discovery Service\n- [ ] B. Migration Evaluator\n- [x] C. AWS Migration Hub\n- [ ] D. AWS Application Migration Service\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Migration Hub is a centralized hub to take the customer through the discovery, assessment, planning, and execution phases of their migration.\n","m06-09-aws-storage-gateway.md":"# Module 6: Storage › AWS Storage Gateway\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m06-09-aws-storage-gateway-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAnyCompany has a large collection of files stored on-premises that needs to be backed up to the AWS Cloud. They want to maintain local access to frequently used files while using cloud storage for cost savings. They also want to minimize changes to their existing file-sharing workflows and applications.Which AWS Storage Gateway type BEST addresses these requirements?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Tape Gateway\n- [x] B. Amazon S3 File Gateway\n- [ ] C. Volume Gateway in Cached mode\n- [ ] D. Volume Gateway in Stored mode\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: S3 File Gateway provides a file interface into Amazon S3 so the team can store and retrieve objects using standard file protocols like NFS and SMB. With S3 File Gateway, frequently accessed data is cached locally for low-latency access while data is stored in Amazon S3 for durability and cost-effectiveness.\n\n<!-- id: m06-09-aws-storage-gateway-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAnyCompany Manufacturing stores CAD files that need to be accessed frequently by engineers at their on-premises data center. They want to maintain local access to this data while also benefiting from AWS Cloud storage capabilities. They plan to implement a solution that provides low-latency access to frequently used files while backing up data to AWS.Which AWS Storage Gateway configuration should they choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Deploy Amazon FSx for Windows File Server in the on-premises data center.\n- [ ] B. Implement Storage Gateway in Stored Volume mode and configure all volumes to be stored entirely in Amazon S3.\n- [ ] C. Implement Storage Gateway in Tape Gateway mode to back up the CAD files to virtual tapes in Amazon S3.\n- [x] D. Implement Storage Gateway in Cached Volume mode to keep frequently accessed data local while storing the complete dataset in Amazon S3.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Cached Volume mode is ideal for this scenario because it stores the most frequently accessed data locally for low-latency access while maintaining the complete dataset in Amazon S3. This provides both the local performance that engineers need and the benefits of secure cloud backup.\n","m03-02-aws-lambda.md":"# Module 3: Exploring Compute Services › AWS Lambda\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m03-02-aws-lambda-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA development team at a fintech startup is building a new customer-facing microservice using AWS Lambda. AWS takes care of the infrastructure, but the team is focused on meeting strict security and compliance requirements. Which task is still the team's responsibility when using Lambda?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Scaling the infrastructure\n- [ ] B. Patching the underlying operating system\n- [ ] C. Managing server availability\n- [x] D. Managing data access permissions\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Although AWS manages the infrastructure, the team is responsible for correctly configuring AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) roles and permissions for any services that the Lambda function accesses.\n\n<!-- id: m03-02-aws-lambda-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA photography company offers cloud-based photo editing and storage. To streamline operations, it uses AWS Lambda to automatically process photos—resizing images, applying filters, and organizing files—every time a client uploads a new image. Which key components are involved in running an automated photo processing workflow with Lambda?\n\n_Choose 3_\n\n- [x] A. Lambda function\n- [x] B. Triggers\n- [ ] C. Server provisioning\n- [x] D. Runtimes\n- [ ] E. Manual scaling configuration\n- [ ] F. Operating system selection\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The key components of AWS Lambda are the function, triggers, and runtimes. These components handle code, respond to events, and provide the language environment. Customers do not need to manage servers, scaling, or operating systems. AWS takes care of all that.\n","m13-03-aws-well-architected-framework.md":"# Module 13: Well-Architected Solutions › AWS Well-Architected Framework\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m13-03-aws-well-architected-framework-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA development team is releasing frequent updates to an application hosted on AWS. Right now, each deployment requires manual steps that often result in downtime or inconsistent environments.What AWS practice from the Well-Architected Framework could help in this situation?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Focus on securing their deployments (Security).\n- [x] B. Automate deployments through a continuous integration and continuous delivery pipeline (Operational Excellence).\n- [ ] C. Reduce the cost of the infrastructure used for deployments (Cost Optimization).\n- [ ] D. Use AWS resources more effectively during deployment (Performance Efficiency).\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Automating deployments with a CI/CD pipeline like AWS CodePipeline would streamline the process, reduce downtime, and help provide more reliable deployments.\n\n<!-- id: m13-03-aws-well-architected-framework-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is the purpose of the AWS Well-Architected Tool (AWS WA Tool)?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. To automate cost forecasting for cloud projects\n- [ ] B. To manage user permissions across AWS services\n- [x] C. To assess and improve cloud workloads based on six key architectural pillars\n- [ ] D. To migrate workloads between AWS Regions\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The AWS WA Tool helps evaluate workloads using the six pillars: Operational Excellence, Security, Reliability, Performance Efficiency, Cost Optimization, and Sustainability.\n","m02-05-amazon-ec2-pricing.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Amazon EC2 Pricing\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-05-amazon-ec2-pricing-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA financial services company needs to run sensitive applications that handle confidential customer data and require compliance with industry regulations. They need complete control over the physical server, including instance placement and resource allocation.Which pricing option should they choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Savings Plans\n- [ ] B. Spot Instances\n- [ ] C. On Demand\n- [x] D. Dedicated Hosts\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Dedicated Hosts provide exclusive use of a physical server, providing full control over placement and resource allocation. This is ideal for security-sensitive and licensing-specific workloads.\n\n<!-- id: m02-05-amazon-ec2-pricing-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA startup is running a batch processing workload that can tolerate occasional interruptions, and they want to reduce costs by taking advantage of unused Amazon EC2 capacity.Which pricing option would offer them the most savings?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Reserved Instances\n- [ ] B. On Demand\n- [x] C. Spot Instances\n- [ ] D. Savings Plans\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Spot Instances offer up to 90 percent off On-Demand pricing, making them the most cost-effective option for workloads that can tolerate interruptions.\n\n<!-- id: m02-05-amazon-ec2-pricing-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA customer is building a new application and is unsure of their usage patterns but expects to grow and stabilize usage over time. They want to start without a long-term commitment.Which pricing option should they use?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Savings Plans\n- [ ] B. Spot Instances\n- [ ] C. Reserved Instances\n- [x] D. On Demand\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: On-Demand pricing is ideal for starting without commitment. The customer can test and adjust based on actual usage before committing to longer-term options.\n","m07-01-introduction-to-databases.md":"# Module 7: Databases › Introduction to Databases\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m07-01-introduction-to-databases-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAnyCompany Logistics is growing and expanding their online platform. The development team must choose between two database options. They can host their own database on an Amazon EC2 instance or use AWS's fully managed database service. The company wants to reduce IT maintenance tasks so their staff can focus more on development work. Which option should they choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Choose a managed database service, because the team wants to focus on developing new features rather than database administration tasks.\n- [ ] B. Choose the self-hosted database on Amazon EC2, because it will always provide better performance for ecommerce applications.\n- [ ] C. Choose the managed database service, because it will automatically optimize the company's application code.\n- [ ] D. Choose the self-hosted database on Amazon EC2, because it is always more cost effective for growing companies.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Fully managed AWS database services handle heavy lifting tasks like backups, patches, and high availability. This lets the development team focus on building application features that drive business value.\n","m02-02-amazon-ec2-instance-types.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Amazon EC2 Instance Types\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-02-amazon-ec2-instance-types-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA financial institution is running a real-time analytics application that processes large datasets stored across multiple servers to provide quick query results. The application requires fast processing of data with a focus on handling large volumes of information efficiently.Which Amazon EC2 instance type would be the BEST choice for this task?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. General purpose\n- [ ] B. Compute optimized\n- [ ] C. Storage optimized\n- [x] D. Memory optimized\n\n<!-- id: m02-02-amazon-ec2-instance-types-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA retail company is setting up a solution to analyze historical sales data that is stored locally. The solution requires fast access to large datasets with consistent, high disk throughput for quick data retrieval.Which Amazon EC2 instance type would be the MOST suitable for this use case?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Compute optimized\n- [x] B. Storage optimized\n- [ ] C. General purpose\n- [ ] D. Accelerated computing\n","m08-04-introduction-to-generative-ai-on-aws.md":"# Module 8: AI/ML and Data Analytics › Introduction to Generative AI on AWS\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m08-04-introduction-to-generative-ai-on-aws-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nGenerative AI is a type of deep learning powered by extremely large ML models that are pre-trained on vast collections of data. What are these models called?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Generative models\n- [ ] B. Massive models\n- [x] C. Foundation models\n- [ ] D. Feature models\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Generative AI is powered by extremely large ML models known as foundation models (FMs). FMs are pre-trained on vast collections of data. FMs can be adapted to perform multiple tasks.\n","m13-05-assessment.md":"# Module 13: Well-Architected Solutions › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m13-05-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA developer is working on a full-stack application hosted on AWS. They are interested in streamlining the development process by quickly adding features like authentication and storage with minimal infrastructure management. Which AWS service would provide the best solution for the developer's needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS AppSync\n- [x] B. AWS Amplify\n- [ ] C. AWS CodePipeline\n- [ ] D. AWS Well-Architected Tool\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amplify streamlines full-stack development by providing ready-to-use authentication, storage, and API components. It requires only minimal infrastructure management.\n\n<!-- id: m13-05-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nThe owner of a large hardware company wants to automate and optimize the company’s marketing emails to enhance customer engagement. Which AWS service would work well for this use case?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES)\n- [ ] B. AWS Amplify\n- [ ] C. Amazon Connect\n- [ ] D. Amazon AppStream 2.0\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon SES provides scalable email sending capability specifically designed for marketing campaigns and customer communications.\n\n<!-- id: m13-05-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA small technology startup needs to provide its remote workforce with secure access to their work environment. The employees must be able to accomplish the same tasks as if they were on a physical office computer. Which AWS service can they use to provide this remote access?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Connect\n- [x] B. Amazon WorkSpaces\n- [ ] C. AWS AppSync\n- [ ] D. Amazon AppStream 2.0\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: WorkSpaces provides a complete persistent desktop experience for remote workers.\n\n<!-- id: m13-05-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA manufacturing company needs a way to monitor its assembly-line equipment for any performance issues. Which AWS service can help them build a monitoring solution for the equipment?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Well-Architected Tool\n- [ ] B. Amazon AppStream 2.0\n- [x] C. AWS IoT Core\n- [ ] D. Amazon Connect\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS IoT Core is specifically designed to connect, monitor, and manage IoT devices like manufacturing equipment.\n\n<!-- id: m13-05-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nA startup is hosting a critical web application on a single Amazon EC2 instance in one Availability Zone. After a brief outage, they decide to reevaluate their architecture. What practice from the AWS Well-Architected Framework could improve this situation?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Reduce resource usage to avoid overprovisioning (Cost Optimization).\n- [ ] B. Scale up the instance to handle more traffic (Performance Efficiency).\n- [ ] C. Increase the instance’s firewall protection (Security).\n- [x] D. Deploy instances across multiple Availability Zones for fault tolerance (Reliability).\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: By deploying instances across multiple Availability Zones, the web application will be more resilient to failures and will have higher availability.\n\n<!-- id: m13-05-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nA company is using a large Amazon EC2 instance type for a low-traffic website, but monitoring shows CPU usage rarely exceeds 10 percent. What is a good next step?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Upgrade the EC2 instance for better data protection.\n- [x] B. Rightsize the EC2 instance to a smaller type to match the actual workload.\n- [ ] C. Decrease the number of instances to save money.\n- [ ] D. Automate the scaling of EC2 instances based on traffic.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Rightsizing the EC2 instance to a smaller type that fits the actual workload would improve performance efficiency by avoiding resource wastage.\n","m12-08-assessment.md":"# Module 12: Migrating to the AWS Cloud › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m12-08-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nThe migration team wants to make sure the organization considers a company-wide change management strategy for successful cloud adoption. Which Cloud Adoption Framework (CAF) perspective would they use?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Operations\n- [ ] B. Business\n- [x] C. People\n- [ ] D. Security\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The People perspective supports development of an organization-wide change management strategy for successful cloud adoption.\n\n<!-- id: m12-08-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is the primary function of the AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF)?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. It provides tools to help accelerate the migration journey, organize resources, and align management during the transition.\n- [ ] B. It acts as a centralized hub to manage a company's migration to the AWS Cloud.\n- [ ] C. It migrates on-premises databases and data to the AWS Cloud.\n- [ ] D. It is also known as the seven Rs or the seven migration strategies.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS CAF provides AWS experience and best practices to companies preparing to migrate to the AWS Cloud. The framework also provides tools to help accelerate the migration journey, organize resources, and align management during the transition.\n\n<!-- id: m12-08-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nWhat are the seven migration strategies that are commonly used when customers migrate to the AWS Cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. There are not seven, there are three (Assess, Mobilize, and Migrate and Modernize)\n- [ ] B. Relocate, Remediate, Retrofit, Refactor, Regrade, Retool, Remove\n- [ ] C. Business, People, Governance, Platform, Security, Operations, IT\n- [x] D. Relocate, Rehost, Replatform, Refactor, Repurchase, Retain, and Retire\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The seven Rs, or migration strategies, are Relocate, Rehost, Replatform, Refactor, Repurchase, Retain, and Retire.\n\n<!-- id: m12-08-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA retail company is just getting started with their migration to the AWS Cloud. They need help building a business case to secure funding from their chief financial officer (CFO) and stakeholders. Which migration service would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Migration Evaluator\n- [ ] B. AWS Application Migration Service\n- [ ] C. AWS Application Discovery Service\n- [ ] D. AWS Migration Hub\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Migration Evaluator is a migration assessment service that helps the company create a business case for AWS Cloud planning and migration.\n\n<!-- id: m12-08-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nA media company is in the migrate and modernize phase of their migration and wants a centralized location to view their migration tasks and progress.Which migration service would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Migration Hub\n- [ ] B. Migration Evaluator\n- [ ] C. AWS Application Discovery Service\n- [ ] D. AWS Application Migration Service\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Migration Hub is a centralized hub that takes the company through the discovery, assessment, planning, and implementation phases of migration.\n\n<!-- id: m12-08-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nAn environmental agency is migrating their applications to the AWS Cloud. During the migration they also want to look for ways to modernize and reduce costs of their applications.Which migration service would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Migration Evaluator\n- [ ] B. AWS Application Discovery Service\n- [x] C. AWS Application Migration Service\n- [ ] D. AWS Migration Hub\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Application Migration Service is a tool to migrate and improve on-premises and cloud-based applications. It helps the agency simplify, expedite, and reduce the cost of migrating and modernizing applications.\n\n<!-- id: m12-08-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nDuring their upcoming migration, the database administrator would like to move from their current database to an AWS managed database to offload some of the database administration. They would also like to use a tool to plan, assess, convert, and migrate the database.Which migration solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Migration Hub\n- [ ] B. AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT)\n- [x] C. AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS)\n- [ ] D. Migration Evaluator\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Database Migration Service makes it possible to quickly and securely migrate databases and data replication to the AWS Cloud. It provides a way to plan, assess, convert, and migrate databases even with data warehouses in one central tool and can be used when converting databases.\n\n<!-- id: m12-08-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nA credit card company is migrating large amounts of sensitive data from their on-premises storage to the AWS Cloud. They want to automate the process and schedule the migration during off peak times. They also want to be able to check on progress and task reporting. They do not have a dedicated private connection between their data center and the AWS Cloud.Which online migration solution would meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Transfer Family\n- [x] B. AWS DataSync\n- [ ] C. AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized Devices\n- [ ] D. Virtual private gateway\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: DataSync is an online migration service specifically designed for automating and accelerating data transfer. DataSync streamlines and accelerates moving large amounts of data between on-premises storage and AWS storage services like Amazon S3, Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS), and Amazon FSx for Windows File Server.\n\n<!-- id: m12-08-assessment-q9 -->\n## Question 9\n\nAn engineering company is migrating large amounts of proprietary intellectual property design files from their on-premises data center to the AWS Cloud. They want a service that has fully managed support for secure file transfers with several different protocols, like Secure File Transfer Protocol (SFTP) and File Transfer Protocol Secure (FTPS)Which online migration solution would meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS DataSync\n- [ ] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] C. AWS Snowball Edge Storage Optimized Devices\n- [x] D. AWS Transfer Family\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Transfer Family makes it possible to seamlessly manage and share data with secure, and scalable file transfers. This service provides fully managed support for secure file transfers over SFTP (Secure File Transfer Protocol), FTPS (File Transfer Protocol Secure), FTP (File Transfer Protocol) and others.\n","m10-08-governance.md":"# Module 10: Monitoring, Compliance, and Governance in the AWS Cloud › Governance\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m10-08-governance-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA government customer needs to set up and govern a secure, compliant, multi-account AWS environment. They want to make sure that employees comply with their approved requirements when creating new AWS accounts.Which AWS service would best fit the customer's need?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS CloudTrail\n- [ ] B. AWS License Manager\n- [ ] C. AWS Service Catalog\n- [x] D. AWS Control Tower\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Control Tower will help with the configuration of new accounts. The customer can use it to enforce and manage governance rules for security, operations, and compliance at scale across all their organizations and accounts in the AWS Cloud.\n","m12-06-transferring-data-online.md":"# Module 12: Migrating to the AWS Cloud › Transferring Data Online\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m12-06-transferring-data-online-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA healthcare company is migrating large amounts of data between their on-premises storage in Amazon S3. They want to automate the process and be able to schedule the migration to off-peak times and be able to check on progress and task reporting.Which service would best meet their need to transfer the data?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] B. Transfer using the internet, no AWS service needed\n- [ ] C. AWS Transfer Family\n- [x] D. AWS DataSync\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: DataSync streamlines and accelerate secure data migrations. It manages data movement workloads with bandwidth throttling, migration scheduling, task filtering, and task reporting.\n","m11-02-aws-pricing-concepts.md":"# Module 11: Pricing and Support › AWS Pricing Concepts\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m11-02-aws-pricing-concepts-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou work as a cloud engineer for a health care company. The chief technology officer wants to store patient records in the cloud. They ask you about the driving factors of cost. Which answer BEST describes the key driving factors of cost for the AWS Cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The primary driving factors of cost are compute, storage, database, networking, and migration and transfer.\n- [ ] B. The only driving factor of cost is compute.\n- [x] C. Although pricing factors into multiple service categories, the primary driving factors of cost are compute, storage, and data transfer.\n- [ ] D. The only driving factor of cost is storage.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Pricing factors into numerous service categories, but the driving factors of cost are compute, storage, and data transfer.\n","m01-04-introduction-to-aws-global-infrastructure.md":"# Module 1: Introduction to the Cloud › Introduction to AWS Global Infrastructure\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m01-04-introduction-to-aws-global-infrastructure-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou just joined a tech start-up, and the business is growing rapidly. Your new company decides that they need to design a resilient and scalable infrastructure on AWS to handle increased traffic and help ensure high availability.Which statement BEST describes the AWS Global Infrastructure benefit of high availability?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS has many customer support options to make sure the answers to your questions are highly available on its website.\n- [x] B. AWS provides multiple data centers across different geographic regions so your website can remain operational even if one location faces issues.\n- [ ] C. AWS offers a single, highly secure data center that can handle all your traffic, which makes sure that your website is available.\n- [ ] D. AWS stores all of your website’s data in a single AWS storage bucket to centralize data management.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS does provide multiple data centers across different geographic regions. This setup enhances high availability by making sure that your online store can handle increased traffic even during unforeseen events.\n","m08-05-aws-generative-ai-solutions.md":"# Module 8: AI/ML and Data Analytics › AWS Generative AI Solutions\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m08-05-aws-generative-ai-solutions-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA large advertising agency wants to quickly integrate a new content generation feature into its existing enterprise-wide design application. The new feature needs to be able to generate both text and images. The agency doesn't want to manage any new infrastructure. Which service would work best for this use case?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon Bedrock\n- [ ] B. Amazon SageMaker JumpStart\n- [ ] C. Amazon Q Developer\n- [ ] D. Amazon Q Business\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Bedrock would work well for fully managed, enterprise-grade, multimodal generative AI.\n\n<!-- id: m08-05-aws-generative-ai-solutions-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA software development company is working on a new product with a very tight deadline. The company needs a way to develop code faster without sacrificing reliability or security. Which service could best help this company meet its deadline?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Bedrock\n- [ ] B. Amazon SageMaker JumpStart\n- [x] C. Amazon Q Developer\n- [ ] D. Amazon Q Business\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Q Developer provides code recommendations to accelerate development of C#, Java, JavaScript, Python, and TypeScript applications. It's a good fit for this use case.\n","m11-04-aws-support-plans.md":"# Module 11: Pricing and Support › AWS Support Plans\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m11-04-aws-support-plans-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA large organization is trying to decide the level of AWS Support that best suits their needs. The company has the following requirements:Basic AWS Trusted Advisor security checks15-minute response time for business-critical system down scenariosFull set of AWS Trusted Advisor checks and prioritized recommendations by an AWS account team. A dedicated Technical Account Manager (TAM) for consultative architectural and operational guidance. Which AWS Support Plan should the company choose based on these requirements?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Business Support\n- [x] B. Enterprise Support\n- [ ] C. Developer Support\n- [ ] D. Basic Support\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Enterprise Support is ideal for large organizations needing 15-minute response times and a dedicated technical account manager for consultative architectural and operational guidance.\n","m10-05-compliance.md":"# Module 10: Monitoring, Compliance, and Governance in the AWS Cloud › Compliance\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m10-05-compliance-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhich tasks can you complete in AWS Artifact? (Select TWO.)\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [x] A. Access AWS compliance reports on demand.\n- [ ] B. Consolidate and manage multiple AWS accounts within a central location.\n- [ ] C. Create users to permit people and applications to interact with AWS services and resources.\n- [ ] D. Set permissions for accounts by configuring service control policies (SCPs).\n- [x] E. Review, accept, and manage agreements with AWS.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AW\n","m10-10-aws-trusted-advisor.md":"# Module 10: Monitoring, Compliance, and Governance in the AWS Cloud › AWS Trusted Advisor\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m10-10-aws-trusted-advisor-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAn enterprise customer with a multi-Region AWS network is looking for ways to continuously evaluate and reduce costs while making sure that everything is secure and performing efficiently. They are also interested in learning AWS best practices to apply to their operations.Which solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Identity and Access Management Access Analyzer\n- [ ] B. Amazon Inspector\n- [ ] C. AWS Shared Responsibility Model\n- [x] D. AWS Trusted Advisor\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Trusted Advisor would continuously evaluate and provide recommendations on cost, security, and performance. It would also provide recommendations on best practices.\n","m08-03-aws-ai-ml-solutions.md":"# Module 8: AI/ML and Data Analytics › AWS AI/ML Solutions\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m08-03-aws-ai-ml-solutions-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nThe owner of a car dealership wants to determine why her service department has lost business over the past year. She wants to analyze a large number of documented customer comments to better understand customer sentiment. Which AWS service would work well for this use case?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Translate\n- [ ] B. Amazon Textract\n- [ ] C. Amazon Personalize\n- [x] D. Amazon Comprehend\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Comprehend can extract key insights, such as customer sentiment, from documents. This can help the owner better understand her customers.\n\n<!-- id: m08-03-aws-ai-ml-solutions-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA healthcare company wants to add a conversational interface to its customer support application using a ready-made solution. Which AWS service could they choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon Lex\n- [ ] B. Amazon Comprehend\n- [ ] C. Amazon Translate\n- [ ] D. Amazon Personalize\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With Amazon Lex, the company can add voice and text conversational interfaces to their applications to create lifelike conversations. It can enhance the healthcare company's customer support app.\n\n<!-- id: m08-03-aws-ai-ml-solutions-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nAn instructional designer is developing a new course on customer service skills. He wants to include several simulated calls to reinforce the learning. Because he doesn't have access to a recording studio, he needs a quick way to convert his scripts to speech. Which service would work well for this use case?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Textract\n- [ ] B. Amazon Kendra\n- [ ] C. Amazon Translate\n- [x] D. Amazon Polly\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Polly converts text into lifelike speech. It supports multiple languages, different genders, and a variety of accents. It is an ideal match for this use case.\n\n<!-- id: m08-03-aws-ai-ml-solutions-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA small tech company wants to develop their own customized machine learning (ML) model without managing the underlying infrastructure. The company is looking for a solution that both their data scientists and business analysts can use. Which AWS service should they choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon EC2\n- [x] B. Amazon SageMaker AI\n- [ ] C. Amazon Kendra\n- [ ] D. Amazon Lex\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: They can use SageMaker AI to develop their ML models without worrying about infrastructure. Data scientists can use the IDE, and business analysts can use the no-code interface.\n\n<!-- id: m08-03-aws-ai-ml-solutions-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nA team of machine learning (ML) engineers is developing a new ML model for a highly specialized application. They need complete control over the ML training process. So, they are developing their own custom solution using the PyTorch ML framework. What is an ML framework?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. A software library with pre-built, optimized components\n- [ ] B. A managed service pre-trained to perform specific functions\n- [ ] C. An integrated development environment (IDE) that provides simplified access to the company's ML projects\n- [ ] D. An Amazon EC2 instance that is optimized for ML training\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: An ML framework is a software library or tool that provides experienced ML practitioners with pre-built, optimized components for building machine learning models.\n","m05-04-subnets-security-groups-and-network-access-control-lists.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Subnets, Security Groups, and Network Access Control Lists\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-04-subnets-security-groups-and-network-access-control-lists-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA retail customer is setting up their application in the AWS Cloud. The application requires a lot of control in defining traffic rules for the individual Amazon EC2 instances in their public subnet. Which solution would BEST meet the requirements for securing the resources?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Change all the subnets to private subnets to avoid accessing from the public internet.\n- [ ] B. Set up network ACLs for the EC2 instances based on the application requirements.\n- [x] C. Set up security groups for the EC2 instances based on the application requirements.\n- [ ] D. Set up a public subnet with strong passwords that meet the customer's requirements.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Security groups would allow the fine-grained control at the instance level.\n\n<!-- id: m05-04-subnets-security-groups-and-network-access-control-lists-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhich network component performs stateless packet filtering?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Network access control list (network ACL)\n- [ ] B. Security groups\n- [ ] C. Amazon VPC\n- [ ] D. Private subnet\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Network access control lists are stateless and don't remember the previous decisions made for incoming packets.\n","m02-09-assessment.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhich option BEST describes how compute resources are provisioned and managed in the cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Resources are provisioned based on demand, allowing for scaling and management.\n- [ ] B. Compute resources are fixed and cannot be scaled.\n- [ ] C. Compute resources require constant manual management.\n- [ ] D. Resources must be pre-purchased and installed onsite.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Cloud computing resources are dynamic and can be adjusted in real-time to meet changing demand, allowing for easier scaling and management.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA media company is working on a project that involves rendering complex visual effects and simulations. The rendering process requires significant computational power and hardware accelerators to handle the intense workload efficiently.Which Amazon EC2 instance type would be the BEST choice for this task?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Compute optimized\n- [ ] B. General purpose\n- [x] C. Accelerated computing\n- [ ] D. Memory optimized\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Accelerated computing instances are equipped with GPUs and hardware accelerators, making them ideal for rendering tasks that require high computational power and efficiency.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA startup company is building a new web application and chooses general purpose Amazon EC2 instances to host the application.Why did they choose this instance type?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It provides the highest performance for compute-heavy tasks, such as video rendering or machine learning.\n- [ ] B. It is designed for high storage capacity, which is needed to host large databases.\n- [x] C. It provides a balanced mix of compute, memory, and networking resources while keeping costs efficient as they scale their user base.\n- [ ] D. It is specifically designed for memory-intensive applications, which is ideal for hosting a web application.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: General purpose instances offer a good balance of resources for various types of workloads, including web applications, making them a flexible and cost-effective choice.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA university research team is running climate modeling simulations that require substantial CPU power to process complex algorithms and analyze large datasets.Why are compute optimized Amazon EC2 instances ideal for this task?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. They are ideal for tasks that require significant CPU power to perform computations.\n- [ ] B. They are designed for workloads that require a high amount of memory to process large datasets efficiently.\n- [ ] C. They are optimized for handling tasks that require hardware accelerators.\n- [ ] D. They provide high storage throughput, making them ideal for tasks that require fast data retrieval and storage for large datasets.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Compute optimized instances are specifically designed for compute-heavy workloads like simulations, offering higher CPU performance to process complex algorithms and analyze large datasets.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nWhat does multi-tenancy refer to in the context of Amazon EC2?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. EC2 instances dedicated to individual clients\n- [ ] B. Instances that are restricted to one geographical region\n- [x] C. Multiple users sharing the same EC2 instance while maintaining isolation\n- [ ] D. Each EC2 instance running in its own private network\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Multi-tenancy in Amazon EC2 refers to multiple tenants, or users, sharing the same instance but maintaining isolation for security and performance.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nWhich tool can be used to interact with AWS services through a graphical user interface (GUI)?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Software Development Kit (AWS SDK)\n- [ ] B. Amazon EC2\n- [x] C. AWS Management Console\n- [ ] D. AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The AWS Management Console is the web-based GUI that is used to interact with AWS services.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nA company has critical steady-state workloads and batch jobs that are not time-sensitive.How should they optimize costs using Amazon EC2 Savings Plans and Spot Instances?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Use Savings Plans for critical workloads and Spot Instances for jobs that are not time-sensitive to maximize savings.\n- [ ] B. Use Savings Plans for non-time-sensitive workloads and Spot Instances for critical jobs.\n- [ ] C. Use Spot Instances for all workloads to maximize savings and avoid Savings Plans.\n- [ ] D. Use Savings Plans for all workloads and avoid Spot Instances because of interruption risks.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This is the best approach. Savings Plans are ideal for critical workloads that need consistent capacity and predictable pricing. Spot Instances offer significant savings for jobs that are not time-sensitive and can tolerate interruptions.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nA marketing agency is developing a new web application and expects steady growth, but is unsure of traffic in the early months. They want flexibility without a long-term commitment.Which pricing option should they use?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Savings Plans\n- [ ] B. Reserved Instances\n- [ ] C. Spot Instances\n- [x] D. On-Demand\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: On-Demand pricing is ideal for starting without commitment. The customer can test and adjust based on actual usage before committing to longer-term options.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q9 -->\n## Question 9\n\nA manufacturing company is running a set of predictable workloads for the next 3 years and wants to optimize costs.Which option should they choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. On-Demand\n- [ ] B. Spot Instances\n- [ ] C. Dedicated Hosts\n- [x] D. Reserved Instances\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Reserved Instances offer up to a 75 percent discount for steady-state, predictable workloads when committing to a 1-year or 3-year term, making them the most cost-effective option.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q10 -->\n## Question 10\n\nWhat is the primary role of an Amazon Machine Image (AMI) when scaling applications?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It stores backup copies of application data.\n- [ ] B. It configures scaling policies for applications.\n- [ ] C. It automatically manages network traffic.\n- [x] D. It provides a consistent image to launch new instances.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AMIs launch new Amazon EC2 instances with the same software configuration and settings, providing consistency.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q11 -->\n## Question 11\n\nHow does Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling work in AWS?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling adjusts the instance type but does not change the number of instances.\n- [ ] B. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling requires manual intervention to add or remove instances based on traffic.\n- [ ] C. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling adds instances when the workload is too high, but it does not scale down when demand decreases.\n- [x] D. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling automatically adds or removes instances based on performance data and application metrics.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: For optimal resource usage, Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling automatically adjusts the number of instances based on performance metrics.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q12 -->\n## Question 12\n\nHow do Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling and Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) work together in AWS?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. They operate independently and are not connected.\n- [ ] B. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling handles traffic routing, whereas ELB manages instance scaling.\n- [ ] C. ELB automatically scales the EC2 instances, and Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling adjusts traffic.\n- [x] D. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling adjusts the number of instances, whereas ELB distributes traffic evenly across them.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances in response to changes in demand. ELB distributes incoming traffic evenly across those instances, supporting high availability and reliability.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q13 -->\n## Question 13\n\nWhat happens if one component fails in a loosely coupled architecture?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The system automatically switches to backup components without any intervention.\n- [x] B. The system can continue to function as other components are independent.\n- [ ] C. The failure causes the entire system to fail.\n- [ ] D. Other components must be manually restarted.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Loosely coupled systems are designed so that components are independent. If one component fails, the rest of the system can continue to function normally, minimizing the impact of the failure.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q14 -->\n## Question 14\n\nA software development company needs to notify the engineering team whenever a new bug is reported in their bug tracking system. Some team members need to be notified immediately, whereas others can process the bug reports later.Which service should the software development company choose based on the requirements?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS)\n- [x] B. Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS)\n- [ ] C. Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)\n- [ ] D. Amazon EC2\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon SNS is the better choice because it delivers notifications in real time to multiple recipients simultaneously. This suits the need for immediate notifications to engineers about new bugs.\n","m04-04-infrastructure-and-automation.md":"# Module 4: Going Global › Infrastructure and Automation\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m04-04-infrastructure-and-automation-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA rapidly growing tech startup company is planning to launch a new web application that will require a complex infrastructure setup, including multiple Amazon EC2 instances, Elastic Load Balancing, and Auto Scaling groups. The application must be deployed consistently across different environments. Would AWS CloudFormation be a good solution for managing the company's infrastructure?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. CloudFormation should be used only for setting up static websites, not for complex applications.\n- [ ] B. CloudFormation is too complicated and would slow down the deployment process.\n- [x] C. CloudFormation would be ideal because it supports infrastructure as code (IaC), enabling consistent, repeatable deployments across different environments.\n- [ ] D. CloudFormation would not be useful in this scenario because it only supports simple infrastructure setups.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: CloudFormation is designed to handle complex infrastructure setups. It defines infrastructure as code to help make sure that deployments are consistent across different environments such as development, testing, and production.\n","m02-04-demo-launching-an-amazon-ec2-instance.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Demo: Launching an Amazon EC2 Instance\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-04-demo-launching-an-amazon-ec2-instance-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat are the required configurations when launching an Amazon EC2 instance for a web server? (Select THREE.)\n\n_Choose 3_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon Machine Image (AMI)\n- [ ] B. Load balancing\n- [x] C. Instance type\n- [ ] D. Permissions\n- [x] E. Storage\n- [ ] F. Instance termination behavior\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: To launch an EC2 instance for a web server, configure the AMI to define the operating system and software; select the instance type to allocate CPU, memory, and storage; and set up storage options, including the type and size of the volume.Load balancing, permissions, and instance termination behavior are not required when launching a basic Amazon EC2 web server.\n\n<!-- id: m02-04-demo-launching-an-amazon-ec2-instance-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is an Amazon Machine Image (AMI) used for when launching an Amazon EC2 instance?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. To choose the instance size\n- [x] B. To pre-configure the operating system and software\n- [ ] C. To store instance data\n- [ ] D. To configure networking settings\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: An AMI is a pre-configured virtual machine image that contains the operating system, application server, and applications. This helps to launch EC2 instances quickly with the desired software and settings.\n","m07-07-assessment.md":"# Module 7: Databases › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhich explanation BEST describes Amazon RDS?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. A fully managed service that helps set up, operate, and scale relational databases in the cloud\n- [ ] B. A fully managed in-memory caching service that seamlessly integrates with Redis, Valkey, or Memcached\n- [ ] C. A data warehousing solution for analytical processing\n- [ ] D. A NoSQL database system optimized for unstructured data\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon RDS is a fully managed database service in the AWS Cloud that frees users from most management tasks and helps set up, operate, and scale databases in the cloud.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is a possible use case for Amazon Aurora?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Replacing high-cost commercial database engines with a more cost-effective solution that still provides enterprise-level performance and reliability\n- [ ] B. Processing unstructured data streams in real time without relational database constraints\n- [ ] C. Storing static, rarely accessed data that requires minimal processing capabilities\n- [ ] D. Running temporary databases with minimal availability requirements for development environments\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Aurora provides comparable performance to high-end commercial databases but at one-tenth the cost, which makes it ideal for organizations looking to reduce database costs without sacrificing performance.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nWhich problem does AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) solve?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Creating automated database backup schedules\n- [x] B. Minimizing application downtime during database migrations\n- [ ] C. Optimizing SQL queries to improve database performance\n- [ ] D. Providing a graphical interface for database administrators to design tables\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A key benefit of AWS DMS is that the source database remains fully operational during migration, which minimizes downtime to applications.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nWhich statement BEST describes Amazon DynamoDB?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. DynamoDB is a relational database service that provides complex SQL query capabilities.\n- [x] B. DynamoDB is a fully managed NoSQL key-value and document database that provides fast, predictable performance with seamless scalability.\n- [ ] C. DynamoDB is a column-oriented database that requires schema definition before storing data.\n- [ ] D. DynamoDB is a fully managed graph database that requires server maintenance during scheduled downtime.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: DynamoDB is a fully managed NoSQL database service that offers both key-value and document data models with predictable, fast performance even at scale.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nWhat is a primary benefit of using Amazon ElastiCache?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Complete replacement for relational databases\n- [ ] B. Automatic scaling of underlying database storage\n- [ ] C. Built-in machine learning capabilities for data analysis\n- [x] D. Improved application performance through in-memory caching\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The core function of ElastiCache is to provide in-memory caching that makes it possible for applications to retrieve data from fast memory stores instead of slower disk-based databases. This significantly reduces latency and improves overall application performance.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nWhat is a feature of AWS Backup?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Backup can only back up resources within a single AWS Region.\n- [ ] B. AWS Backup is limited to database services only.\n- [x] C. AWS Backup provides centralized backup policies and monitoring across multiple AWS accounts and Regions.\n- [ ] D. AWS Backup requires manual configuration for each individual resource.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With AWS Backup, you can define and manage backup policies at the organization level and implement them across all related AWS accounts and Regions automatically.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nWhat is a practical use case for Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility)?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Long-term archival storage of historical data with infrequent access patterns\n- [ ] B. Running high-performance transactional banking applications with strict compliance requirements\n- [x] C. Storing and managing a large product catalog for an ecommerce application\n- [ ] D. Real-time in-memory caching of web session data\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon DocumentDB excels at handling semistructured data like product catalogs.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nWhat is a practical use of Amazon Neptune?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Providing real-time streaming analytics\n- [ ] B. Replacing traditional SQL databases for all workloads\n- [ ] C. Optimizing text search in large document databases\n- [x] D. Managing and querying highly connected datasets efficiently\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Neptune is optimized for storing and querying highly connected data with millisecond latency.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q9 -->\n## Question 9\n\nWhich definition BEST describes in-memory caching?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. A networking solution that optimizes internet routing paths to reduce latency between user requests and cloud-based applications\n- [ ] B. A database management system that permanently stores all application data on solid-state drives for consistent retrieval speeds\n- [x] C. A cloud-based service that stores data in memory for fast access, improving application performance and scalability while reducing database load\n- [ ] D. A backup and recovery service that automatically creates snapshots of critical data every five minutes to prevent data loss\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: In-memory caching is a service that stores frequently used data in memory to improve application performance and reduce the need to fetch data from slower disk-based storage.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q10 -->\n## Question 10\n\nWhat is the primary way that NoSQL databases like Amazon DynamoDB differ from relational databases?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Relational databases offer better performance for transactional workloads than any NoSQL solution.\n- [x] B. NoSQL databases use flexible schema designs rather than the rigid table structures of relational databases.\n- [ ] C. Relational databases require indexes on all queries, and NoSQL databases do not use indexes.\n- [ ] D. Relational databases provide automatic scaling and NoSQL databases require manual scaling.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The key differentiator is that NoSQL databases offer flexible schemas that allow data to be structured in ways beyond the traditional table-based approach. This makes it possible for developers to store and process data in formats that match how their applications use it.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q11 -->\n## Question 11\n\nWhich option describes a scenario where an unmanaged solution like a database installed directly onto an Amazon EC2 instance would be preferable to using a fully managed AWS database service?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. A developer has a database size smaller than the maximum limits imposed by Amazon RDS.\n- [ ] B. A developer wants to scale a database instance based on workload patterns without worrying about licensing complications.\n- [x] C. A developer needs full control over the database and access to its underlying operating system, database installation, and configuration.\n- [ ] D. A developer wants AWS to handle routine database maintenance tasks like backups and patching.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Installing a database directly on Amazon EC2 is preferable when complete administrative control over the entire database environment is needed. This includes operating-system-level access and full configuration flexibility, which is not available in managed AWS services.\n\n<!-- id: m07-07-assessment-q12 -->\n## Question 12\n\nWhich statement describes the responsibilities of customers using fully managed AWS database services?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Customers are responsible for deploying and managing antivirus solutions on the operating systems of fully managed database services.\n- [ ] B. Customers are responsible for provisioning, scaling, patching, and backups.\n- [x] C. Customers are responsible for designing data structures and managing access controls.\n- [ ] D. Customers are responsible for monitoring and generating metrics for their data.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Fully managed AWS database services only require customers to be responsible for designing data structures and managing access controls.\n","m05-08-assessment.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat is networking in the AWS Cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Interconnected devices that can exchange data and resources\n- [ ] B. Physically isolated data centers or set of data centers within an AWS Region\n- [ ] C. Logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define\n- [ ] D. System that translates readable domain names to IP addresses\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: You can think of networking in the AWS Cloud as the infrastructure and services working together to host your applications, data, and any other resources you might need.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is the primary function of an Availability Zone in the AWS Cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It filters inbound and outbound traffic to EC2 instances in a VPC.\n- [ ] B. It provisions a logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define.\n- [ ] C. It allows you to create a subsection of a virtual private cloud (VPC) where you can isolate resources and control access.\n- [x] D. It enhances application availability and fault tolerance by allowing resources to be deployed across multiple zones.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: An Availability Zone is a physically isolated data center or set of data centers within an AWS Region. Each AZ has independent power, cooling, and networking, designed to enhance application availability and fault tolerance by allowing resources to be deployed across multiple Availability Zones within the same Region.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA company wants to establish a secure, private connection between their on-premises data center and their Amazon VPC to create a hybrid cloud architecture.Which component should they use to help ensure a secure connection?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Virtual private gateway\n- [ ] B. Internet gateway\n- [ ] C. Subnet\n- [ ] D. Route table\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A virtual private gateway is the virtual private network (VPN) endpoint on the AWS side. It provides a way for you to establish a secure, encrypted connection between your on-premises network and your virtual private cloud (VPC).\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA customer is creating an Amazon VPC for their application. They want to create a private segment in the Amazon VPC so that resources launched can be isolated from users on the internet.Which network component would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. A private subnet\n- [ ] B. An Availability Zone instead of a subnet\n- [ ] C. A public subnet\n- [ ] D. Either a public subnet or a private subnet would work\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A private subnet is a network segment within a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) that does not have a direct route to the internet. This would meet their needs for the application.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nA retail customer is hosting their application in an Amazon VPC and wants to configure traffic rules for the Amazon EC2 instances running in a public subnet. The application requires multiple rules to be defined at the instance level. Which solution or feature would meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Set up security groups for the Amazon EC2 instances based on the application requirements.\n- [ ] B. Set up a virtual private gateway based on the application requirements.\n- [ ] C. Set up network access control lists, (network ACLs) for the Amazon EC2 instances based on the application requirements.\n- [ ] D. Change the public subnet to a private subnet to avoid public internet access.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Security groups would allow the fine-grained control at the instance level. They can define rules in the public subnet for the individual instances.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nA customer is moving their application to an Amazon VPC and wants to setup a traffic control at the subnet level. They need broad control of traffic in and out and would like to use both allow and deny type rules.Which solution or feature would meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Change the public subnet to a private subnet to avoid public internet access.\n- [ ] B. Set up a virtual private gateway based on the application requirements.\n- [ ] C. Use security groups.\n- [x] D. Use network access control lists (network ACLs).\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Network ACLs would allow the broad traffic control at the subnet level. Network ACLs also have both allow and deny type rules.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nA customer is exploring solutions to establish secure, encrypted connections between their on-premises networks at their data centers and branch offices. They are looking for the MOST cost-effective way to connect their office sites to other sites and their AWS services. They are not looking to increase the amount of bandwidth.Which solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS PrivateLink\n- [ ] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [x] C. AWS Site-to-Site VPN\n- [ ] D. AWS Client VPN\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Site-to-Site VPN creates a secure connection between your data center or branch offices and your AWS Cloud resources.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nAn enterprise customer just merged with another company and needs a way to quickly scale and provide a way for the new worldwide sales force to access their AWS resources. They want a fully managed service with advanced authentication for their new remote workers.Which solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Site-to-Site VPN\n- [ ] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] C. AWS PrivateLink\n- [x] D. AWS Client VPN\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Client VPN is a networking service you can use to connect your remote workers and on-premises networks to the cloud. It provides advanced authentication, and elastic and remote access in a fully managed service.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q9 -->\n## Question 9\n\nA customer wants a way to establish a dedicated connection from their on-premises network to an Amazon VPC. They need a solution that provides a more consistent network experience with increased bandwidth.Which type of connection to the AWS Cloud would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Internet gateway\n- [x] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] C. Amazon CloudFront\n- [ ] D. Virtual private gateway\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Direct Connect would establish a dedicated connection from an on-premises network to one or more virtual private clouds (VPCs). It can also reduce network costs, increase bandwidth throughput, and provide a more consistent network experience than internet-based connections.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q10 -->\n## Question 10\n\nWhat is the primary function of a domain name service (DNS)?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It provisions a logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define.\n- [ ] B. It filters inbound and outbound traffic to Amazon EC2 instances in a virtual private cloud (VPC).\n- [x] C. It translates human-readable domain names to machine readable IP addresses.\n- [ ] D. It allows you to create a subsection of a virtual private cloud (VPC) where you can isolate resources and control access.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A DNS translates the domain name into your browser and sends it to a customer DNS resolver. It then asks the company DNS server for the IP address and returns it so the user can reach the website.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q11 -->\n## Question 11\n\nA customer is creating their application resources in their virtual private cloud (VPC) subnets. They want to secure their resources in the cloud, specifically the networking traffic protection tasks.Which component is the customer responsible for, based on the shared responsibility model?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Securing network traffic with the subnets and resources with Network access control lists (network ACLs) and security groups\n- [ ] B. Securing access to the AWS data centers and facilities that run AWS Cloud services\n- [ ] C. Securing the hardware that runs the AWS Cloud services\n- [ ] D. Securing the software that runs the AWS Cloud services\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The customer is responsible for securing the network traffic. They can do this using security groups and network ACLs.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q12 -->\n## Question 12\n\nA financial customer needs a content delivery solution to deliver required training videos and static content to their financial consultants worldwide. They want to make sure the solution provides low latency.Which AWS solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Global Accelerator\n- [ ] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] C. Amazon Route 53\n- [x] D. Amazon CloudFront\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: CloudFront speeds up distribution of your static and dynamic web content to your users. It securely delivers your content with low latency through a worldwide network of data centers called edge locations.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q13 -->\n## Question 13\n\nA media company needs a service to manage their domain registrations with different providers. They will also be using the service to route internet traffic to their resources hosted both in the AWS Cloud and elsewhere.Which AWS solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon Route 53\n- [ ] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] C. AWS Global Accelerator\n- [ ] D. Amazon CloudFront\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Route 53 is a domain name system (DNS) service that manages domain registration, DNS routing, and health checks. It provides reliable and efficient routing of users to your website or applications, whether they are hosted within AWS or elsewhere.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q14 -->\n## Question 14\n\nA customer is exploring edge networking services to improve application availability, performance, and security. They need a solution for traffic routing when something goes wrong in one of their application's locations. Specifically, it takes into account the endpoint health, user location, and policies.Which AWS solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] B. Amazon CloudFront\n- [ ] C. Amazon Route 53\n- [x] D. AWS Global Accelerator\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Global Accelerator is a network service that is designed to improve the availability and performance of applications for global users. It does this by providing static IP addresses, directing traffic over the AWS global network, and routing to optimal endpoints based on health, user location, and policies.\n","m01-05-the-aws-shared-responsibility-model.md":"# Module 1: Introduction to the Cloud › The AWS Shared Responsibility Model\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m01-05-the-aws-shared-responsibility-model-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou work for a startup company that is developing an application in the cloud. A new security update is available for your operating system (OS), and you are tasked with verifying that the OS is patched accordingly. Which statement BEST describes which party is responsible for applying security patches to the OS that is running in the cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The OS vendor applies the patches.\n- [ ] B. AWS is responsible for applying security patches to the OS.\n- [x] C. Your company is responsible applying security patches to the OS.\n- [ ] D. Both AWS and the customer apply separate patches.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The customer is responsible for managing the security configurations and patches for the OS running in the cloud.\n","m04-05-assessment.md":"# Module 4: Going Global › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA nonprofit organization is migrating all of their resources to the AWS Cloud. They are trying to decide which AWS Region to deploy their resources to.Which option lists the factors the organization needs to consider when deciding where to place their cloud resources?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Software licensing, hardware specifications, cloud skillset of staff, and customer reviews\n- [ ] B. Network speed, data encryption, user interface, and storage capacity\n- [x] C. Compliance, proximity to customers, feature availability, and pricing\n- [ ] D. Server uptime, application performance, employee satisfaction, and office location\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: When deciding where to place cloud resources, companies must consider multiple factors. Compliance refers to the Region meeting legal or regulatory requirements. Proximity to customers helps reduce latency and improve user experience. Feature availability makes sure that the required AWS services are supported in the chosen Region. Pricing varies by Region, so cost-efficiency is also a critical factor.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat BEST describes key benefits of using multiple AWS Regions and multiple Availability Zones?\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [x] A. Low latency for end users\n- [ ] B. Enhanced security protocol\n- [ ] C. Increased storage capacity\n- [x] D. High availability and fault tolerance\n- [ ] E. Faster database migration\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: By using multiple AWS Regions, a company can place their resources closer to their end users, which reduces the distance that the data must travel. This results in lower latency and a better user experience. By using multiple Availability Zones within a Region, the company enhances the fault tolerance of their applications. If one zone fails, their application can continue to operate from another zone, maintaining high availability.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nWhich answer BEST describes the purpose and benefits of AWS edge locations?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Edge locations are composed of physical data centers that host the majority of AWS services and applications.\n- [ ] B. Edge locations are intended to provide redundant storage solutions for critical data.\n- [ ] C. Edge locations are used exclusively for running compute-intensive applications and databases.\n- [x] D. Edge locations cache content to deliver data with lower latency and higher transfer speeds to end users.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This answer accurately describes the purpose and benefits of AWS edge locations. They are designed to improve the delivery of content by caching it closer to end users, thus reducing latency and increasing transfer speeds.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nWhich answer BEST describes the relationship between AWS Regions, Availability Zones, and edge locations?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Regions are physical locations around the world where AWS has multiple Availability Zones. Each Availability Zone has one or more edge location.\n- [ ] B. AWS Regions, Availability Zones, and edge locations are all the same thing and are used interchangeably.\n- [ ] C. AWS Regions contain multiple edge locations, and each edge location can have one or more Availability Zones.\n- [x] D. AWS Regions are physical locations around the world where AWS has multiple Availability Zones. Edge locations are located outside of AWS Regions and cache frequently accessed content.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Regions are indeed physical locations around the world where AWS has multiple isolated Availability Zones. Edge locations, on the other hand, are part of the AWS content delivery network (CDN). They are optimized for content delivery, not directly tied to Availability Zones.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nWhich answer describes the key features and benefits of AWS CloudFormation?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. With CloudFormation, users can model and set up their AWS resources using code to automate provisioning and the management of infrastructure. This method can help to reduce errors and maintain consistency across environments.\n- [ ] B. With CloudFormation, users can cache frequently accessed content. That way, users experience lower latency when accessing cloud resources.\n- [ ] C. CloudFormation is a service that provides a visual interface for manually configuring each AWS resource one by one, without the need for any code.\n- [ ] D. CloudFormation is a cost-optimization tool that analyzes the AWS usage and recommends the best practices for reducing a company's AWS bills.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This answer accurately describes the key features and benefits of CloudFormation. It highlights the ability to model and set up resources using code, automate provisioning, reduce errors, and help maintain environment consistency.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nA team at a biomedical tech company is tasked with deploying a new medical application across multiple AWS Regions to help maintain high availability and fault tolerance. The application consists of several components, including a web server, a database, and a message queue. The deployment needs to be consistent and repeatable and should minimize manual errors through automation.Which approach is BEST suited for deploying this application according to the needs of automation and consistency?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Using the AWS Management Console to manually deploy each component in every Region\n- [x] B. Using an Infrastructure as Code (IaC) service such as AWS CloudFormation to deploy the application\n- [ ] C. Combining console and programmatic approaches for different tiers of the application\n- [ ] D. Writing a script to programmatically deploy the application using the cloud provider's API\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With an IaC service like CloudFormation, the team can define their infrastructure in a declarative way. This helps to version, review, and automate the deployment process for consistency and repeatability.\n","m12-03-seven-migration-strategies.md":"# Module 12: Migrating to the AWS Cloud › Seven Migration Strategies\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m12-03-seven-migration-strategies-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhich migration strategy involves moving to a different product?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Retiring\n- [x] B. Repurchasing\n- [ ] C. Replatforming\n- [ ] D. Refactoring\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Public subnets do not have password security for the traffic rules the customer needs.\n","m06-07-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs.md":"# Module 6: Storage › Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m06-07-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAnyCompany Financial needs to implement a new data application that will analyze market data. The application must be able to scale compute resources up or down to match traffic demand while maintaining access to the same datasets. What is a benefit of using Amazon EFS as the storage solution for the application described in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon EFS provides the lowest cost storage option for infrequently accessed financial data.\n- [x] B. Amazon EFS provides elastic storage capacity, automatically scaling up and down as files are added and removed, with no disruption to applications.\n- [ ] C. Amazon EFS provides faster read access than local instance storage for high-frequency trading algorithms.\n- [ ] D. Amazon EFS provides automatic global replication of data, eliminating the need for data backups.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon EFS automatically scales as data is added or removed. This means AnyCompany Financial can scale their compute resources independently while maintaining access to the same elastic file system.\n\n<!-- id: m06-07-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAnyCompany Retail is planning to migrate their on-premises file storage to AWS. They need a solution that allows their global development teams to collaborate on the same set of files simultaneously.Which feature of Amazon EFS makes it a good fit for this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon EFS provides block storage that can be formatted with any file system.\n- [ ] B. Amazon EFS offers single-instance access with high throughput for dedicated processing.\n- [x] C. Amazon EFS provides shared access for thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, with consistent low latencies.\n- [ ] D. Amazon EFS makes it possible to store files in the cloud, but requires manual synchronization between different instances.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon EFS is designed for concurrent shared access from multiple EC2 instances across different Availability Zones with consistent performance. This makes it possible for global teams to collaborate on the same files.\n","m05-02-organizing-aws-cloud-resources.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Organizing AWS Cloud Resources\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-02-organizing-aws-cloud-resources-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA company is setting up their Amazon VPC. They need to connect their corporate data center through the internet with a secure connection. They also want to make sure the resources are isolated from the public. Which solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. A virtual private gateway with a VPN connection and a private subnet in the Amazon VPC\n- [ ] B. An internet gateway with an Amazon VPC and a public subnet\n- [ ] C. An internet gateway with a public subnet holding the resources in the Amazon VPC\n- [ ] D. An internet gateway with an Amazon VPC and no subnets\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A virtual private gateway with a VPN connection would work. And using a private subnet is exactly what they need!\n","m06-10-aws-elastic-disaster-recovery.md":"# Module 6: Storage › AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m06-10-aws-elastic-disaster-recovery-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAnyCompany Telecommunications is concerned about potential downtime after experiencing an outage last quarter. They want to implement a disaster recovery solution for their on-premises server fleet but have limited IT staff. The CEO is particularly concerned about maintaining exact replicas of production servers and minimizing recovery time.What is a key benefit of using AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Continuous block-level replication with frequent backup intervals, providing near-instant recovery of servers at the target AWS Region\n- [ ] B. Elimination of source-side agents by using existing backup software\n- [ ] C. Direct connection to AWS Storage Gateway to accelerate backup and recovery operations\n- [ ] D. Automated creation of separate development and test environments from production backups\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Elastic Disaster Recovery provides continuous block-level replication that maintains exact server replicas with minimal time between backup intervals, enabling rapid recovery when needed.\n","m03-04-additional-compute-services.md":"# Module 3: Exploring Compute Services › Additional Compute Services\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m03-04-additional-compute-services-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA startup is building a web application and wants a simple way to deploy code without managing infrastructure. They need to have auto scaling and monitoring handled for them. Which AWS service should they use?\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Elastic Beanstalk\n- [ ] B. Amazon EC2\n- [x] C. AWS Batch\n- [ ] D. AWS Outposts\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Elastic Beanstalk handles deployment, scaling, and monitoring for web applications with minimal setup. Rationale: AWS Batch is designed for compute-heavy jobs, not web application deployment.\n\n<!-- id: m03-04-additional-compute-services-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA financial company must run workloads on premises because of strict compliance requirements, but it wants to use AWS services and tools consistently across environments. Which service meets their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Elastic Beanstalk\n- [ ] B. AWS Batch\n- [x] C. AWS Outposts\n- [ ] D. Amazon Lightsail\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Outposts extends AWS infrastructure to on-premises environments with consistent tools and APIs.\n","m06-03-amazon-elastic-block-store-amazon-ebs-data-lifecycle.md":"# Module 6: Storage › Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) Data Lifecycle\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m06-03-amazon-elastic-block-store-amazon-ebs-data-lifecycle-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAnyCompany Commerce operates an online trading platform experiencing rapid growth. Their development team frequently needs to create test environments that mirror production for testing new features, but setting up these environments has become time-consuming and error-prone. What is the most significant benefit of using EBS snapshots in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. EBS snapshots enable rapid creation of new volumes from existing data, so you can quickly deploy identical test environments that mirror production.\n- [ ] B. EBS snapshots reduce your storage costs by compressing all data on your EBS volumes by up to 90 percent.\n- [ ] C. EBS snapshots automatically optimize the performance of your EBS volumes by defragmenting data during the snapshot process.\n- [ ] D. EBS snapshots automatically migrate your data to different AWS Regions for improved global access speeds.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: EBS snapshots capture the exact state of a volume at a point in time, making them perfect for creating consistent copies of environments for testing purposes.\n\n<!-- id: m06-03-amazon-elastic-block-store-amazon-ebs-data-lifecycle-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAnyCompany Healthcare manages thousands of EBS volumes containing patient records. They need to ensure that this data is properly backed up, retained according to compliance requirements, and old snapshots are removed to control costs. Which problem does AWS Data Lifecycle Manager primarily solve in this scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Automating the creation, retention, and deletion of EBS snapshots and EBS backed Amazon Machine Images (AMIs) according to a schedule\n- [ ] B. Migrating patient data from on-premises storage to AWS Cloud storage\n- [ ] C. Providing real-time monitoring of EBS volume performance metrics\n- [ ] D. Encrypting sensitive patient data stored on EBS volumes\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager defines lifecycle policies that automate snapshot management based on schedules. This eliminates the need for manual snapshot management.\n","m08-07-data-pipelines-on-aws.md":"# Module 8: AI/ML and Data Analytics › Data Pipelines on AWS\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m08-07-data-pipelines-on-aws-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA data analytics team is creating an automated data pipeline on AWS.Which AWS services could they choose for data ingestion? (Select TWO.)\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Redshift\n- [x] B. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams\n- [ ] C. Amazon EMR\n- [ ] D. AWS Glue Data Catalog\n- [x] E. Amazon Data Firehose\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Kinesis Data Streams can be used to ingest real-time data, and Amazon Data Firehose can be used to ingest near real-time data.\n\n<!-- id: m08-07-data-pipelines-on-aws-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nThe data analytics team must ingest vast amounts of unstructured data into its pipeline. Which AWS service is the BEST choice for storing this data?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Athena\n- [x] B. Amazon S3\n- [ ] C. Amazon Data Firehose\n- [ ] D. Amazon Redshift\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon S3 can store virtually unlimited amounts of unstructured data. This makes it a popular data lake choice and the best storage option for the team.\n\n<!-- id: m08-07-data-pipelines-on-aws-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nWhich AWS service is BEST suited for data processing in a data pipeline?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon QuickSight\n- [ ] B. Amazon S3\n- [x] C. AWS Glue\n- [ ] D. Amazon Data Firehose\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Glue is used to process data by using the AWS Glue Data Catalog as a reference.\n\n<!-- id: m08-07-data-pipelines-on-aws-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nWhich AWS services could the data analytics team choose for data visualization? (Select TWO.)\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Data Firehose\n- [x] B. Amazon QuickSight\n- [ ] C. Amazon Athena\n- [ ] D. AWS Glue\n- [x] E. Amazon OpenSearch Service\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The data analytics team can use both QuickSight and OpenSearch Service to visualize data in a data pipeline.\n","m05-01-introduction-to-networking.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Introduction to Networking\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-01-introduction-to-networking-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat are the uses of a subnet in an Amazon VPC?\n\n_Choose 3_\n\n- [x] A. Can be used to share public resources\n- [x] B. Can be used to organize your resources\n- [ ] C. Can be used to provide high availability because they consist of one or more discrete data centers\n- [ ] D. Can provide a centralized interface for accessing and managing various AWS resources and services\n- [x] E. Can be used to isolate resources and keep them private\n- [ ] F. Can be used as an on-demand and scalable computing capacity in the AWS Cloud\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Subnets are used to organize resources, share resources publicly, or isolate resources to keep them private.\n","m09-07-assessment.md":"# Module 9: Security › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m09-07-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAn employee wants to check their company’s online employee portal to see how many vacation hours they have accrued. Before accessing their personal records, they enter their username and password to log in to the site.What happens during this login process?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Authorization\n- [x] B. Authentication\n- [ ] C. Encryption\n- [ ] D. Detection\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Authentication is the process of verifying the identity of a user by requiring them to provide credentials, such as a username and password.\n\n<!-- id: m09-07-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is the responsibility of AWS under the AWS shared responsibility model?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Encrypting customer data at rest\n- [x] B. Managing physical security of data centers\n- [ ] C. Configuring security groups for Amazon EC2 instances\n- [ ] D. Setting up AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) roles and policies\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS handles all aspects of physical security for data centers, including facility access controls, environmental safeguards, power redundancy, and surveillance systems.\n\n<!-- id: m09-07-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nWith AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) all actions are denied by default. When granting permissions, access should be provided only on a need-to-have basis. What is this concept called?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Default deny policy\n- [ ] B. Permission boundary framework\n- [ ] C. Role-based access control\n- [x] D. Principle of least privilege\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The principle of least privilege dictates that people and systems should be given access only to what they need and nothing else.\n\n<!-- id: m09-07-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nAll AWS accounts are given an AWS account root user. The root user is the account owner and has full permissions to perform any actions.What are some ways to protect this powerful account? (Select TWO.)\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [ ] A. Create multiple root users for redundancy.\n- [ ] B. Delete the root user after setting up AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) users.\n- [x] C. Associate a strong password with the account.\n- [x] D. Turn on multi-factor authentication (MFA).\n- [ ] E. Delegate root user access to others.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: To protect the root user, it's recommended to associate a strong password with the account and turn on MFA. An AWS account can only have one root user. It cannot be deleted, and root user access should never be delegated to others.\n\n<!-- id: m09-07-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nA large marketing firm has a standard set of permissions used to grant designers access to certain Amazon S3 buckets. The firm added a new S3 bucket that all designers need to access. Which AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) control can the firm use to assign permissions that will be inherited by all of its designers?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. IAM group\n- [ ] B. IAM policy\n- [ ] C. IAM user\n- [ ] D. IAM role\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: IAM groups are specifically designed for this scenario. They are used to assign permissions to multiple users at once.\n\n<!-- id: m09-07-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nA technology company is moving some of its resources to AWS. The company wants to provide single sign-on access for its employees on AWS using its existing identity source. Which service can help the company accomplish this?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Secrets Manager\n- [ ] B. AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)\n- [ ] C. AWS Systems Manager\n- [x] D. AWS IAM Identity Center\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: IAM Identity Center is specifically designed to help organizations implement single sign-on for AWS resources using their existing identity providers.\n\n<!-- id: m09-07-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nA small financial services company recently moved its online resources to AWS. The security team was concerned about protection from common, frequently occurring types of distributed denial of service (DDoS) attacks. Which AWS service automatically protects customers at no cost from DDoS attacks?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Shield\n- [ ] B. AWS Systems Manager\n- [ ] C. Amazon Macie\n- [ ] D. AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Shield is a managed DDoS protection service that safeguards applications running on AWS from common, frequently occurring types of DDoS attacks at no cost.\n\n<!-- id: m09-07-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nProtecting sensitive customer data is a vital component of maintaining customer trust. This involves encrypting data at rest and in transit. What is used to encrypt data in transit?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. SSL/TLS certificates\n- [ ] B. Cryptographic keys\n- [ ] C. Multi-factor authentication (MFA)\n- [ ] D. Strong passwords\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: SSL and its successor, TLS, are protocols specifically designed to encrypt data as it moves between systems over networks.\n\n<!-- id: m09-07-assessment-q9 -->\n## Question 9\n\nA security team for a large ecommerce company needs a centralized way to create and manage the encryption keys that protect its data on AWS. Which of these services is the BEST fit for this team?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Macie\n- [ ] B. AWS Certificate Manager (ACM)\n- [x] C. AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS)\n- [ ] D. AWS WAF\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS KMS is specifically designed to create and manage encryption keys.\n\n<!-- id: m09-07-assessment-q10 -->\n## Question 10\n\nA security team for a large software development company needs to check multiple applications for security vulnerabilities and deviations from security best practices. The applications are running on Amazon EC2, AWS Lambda, and in containers. Which AWS service should they choose for the security assessments?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon GuardDuty\n- [x] B. Amazon Inspector\n- [ ] C. AWS Security Hub\n- [ ] D. Amazon Detective\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Inspector is specifically designed for automated vulnerability assessments of applications hosted on AWS.\n","m04-02-choosing-aws-regions.md":"# Module 4: Going Global › Choosing AWS Regions\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m04-02-choosing-aws-regions-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA cloud engineer for a government agency is tasked with selecting an AWS Region to deploy the agency's resources. Which factors are MOST important to consider when selecting a Region?\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [x] A. Any regulatory compliance standards the agency requires\n- [x] B. Proximity to users\n- [ ] C. Number of files stored\n- [ ] D. Personal preference of the chief information officer\n- [ ] E. How recently the Region was constructed\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: When working for a government agency, making sure that the selected Region complies with all relevant government regulations and policies is important. This includes data sovereignty, privacy laws, and other compliance requirements. Proximity to users or data centers is also important. Close proximity reduces latency and improves the performance of applications and services.\n","m09-04-protecting-data.md":"# Module 9: Security › Protecting Data\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m09-04-protecting-data-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhich processes involve locking and unlocking data with a special key so only authorized users can access it?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Tokenization and masking\n- [ ] B. Authentication and authorization\n- [x] C. Encryption and decryption\n- [ ] D. Hashing and salting\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: These processes specifically involve locking (encryption) and unlocking (decryption) data with a special key to make sure only authorized users can access it.\n\n<!-- id: m09-04-protecting-data-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA tax preparation company needs to secure sensitive customer data moving from its database to its web application on AWS. Which of these services can help them secure the data in transit?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Macie\n- [x] B. AWS Certificate Manager (ACM)\n- [ ] C. Amazon DynamoDB\n- [ ] D. Amazon S3\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: ACM centralizes the management of SSL/TLS certificates that provide data encryption in transit.\n","m03-03-containers-and-orchestration-on-aws.md":"# Module 3: Exploring Compute Services › Containers and Orchestration on AWS\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m03-03-containers-and-orchestration-on-aws-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA developer just finished building an application that runs flawlessly on their laptop. However, when their team tries to deploy it in a different environment, it crashes because of missing dependencies and configuration mismatches. How do containers help solve this problem?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. By providing access to multiple operating systems for compatibility testing\n- [ ] B. By automatically scaling the application across multiple cloud providers\n- [x] C. By packaging the application and everything it needs to run into one consistent environment\n- [ ] D. By eliminating the need to write configuration files\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Containers bundle the application with all of its dependencies and configuration, so it runs the same across different environments.\n","m02-06-scaling-amazon-ec2.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Scaling Amazon EC2\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-06-scaling-amazon-ec2-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat is the primary benefit of scalability and elasticity in AWS?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The ability to permanently increase resource capacity for long-term growth\n- [ ] B. The ability to manually adjust resources based on peak usage\n- [x] C. The ability to grow and shrink resources dynamically based on real-time demand\n- [ ] D. The ability to create fixed resources that never change in size\n\n> Correct! Rationale: By using scalability and elasticity, businesses can adjust resources as needed for optimal performance and cost-efficiency.\n\n<!-- id: m02-06-scaling-amazon-ec2-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is the main reason for deploying Amazon EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. To provide high availability by allowing instances in different Availability Zones to handle traffic if one Availability Zone fails\n- [ ] B. To automatically scale instances based on resource usage in each Availability Zone\n- [ ] C. To increase the power and speed of each individual instance\n- [ ] D. To decrease the cost of instances by distributing them evenly across AWS Regions\n\n> Correct! Rationale: By deploying instances across multiple Availability Zones, businesses can avoid service disruption in the event of an Availability Zone failure.\n\n<!-- id: m02-06-scaling-amazon-ec2-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nHow does AWS make sure that a business can meet fluctuating demand without over-provisioning resources?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. By providing fixed resources that are always available\n- [ ] B. By offering resources that are always running, regardless of demand\n- [ ] C. By requiring businesses to purchase excess resources in advance to handle peak demand\n- [x] D. By allowing businesses to provision resources that automatically scale based on demand\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The AWS scalability and elasticity features automatically adjust resources to meet demand, resulting cost-efficiency and performance.\n","m02-01-introduction-to-amazon-ec2.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Introduction to Amazon EC2\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-01-introduction-to-amazon-ec2-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nHow does Amazon EC2 compare to running servers on premises?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It is more expensive but offers more control.\n- [ ] B. It requires more time to set up and maintain.\n- [ ] C. It is only useful for large businesses.\n- [x] D. It is more flexible, cost-effective, and quicker to get started.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon EC2 is designed to be flexible, cost-effective, and quick to set up compared to on-premises servers.\n\n<!-- id: m02-01-introduction-to-amazon-ec2-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is multi-tenancy in the context of Amazon EC2 instances?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Each virtual machine is isolated but shares resources from a host machine.\n- [ ] B. A server can only run one type of application.\n- [ ] C. Only one user can use the instance at a time.\n- [ ] D. Multiple servers run in the same data center.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Multi-tenancy allows multiple virtual machines to share resources on the same physical host, with isolation between them.\n\n<!-- id: m02-01-introduction-to-amazon-ec2-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA company uses Amazon EC2 instances to deploy their application. What would happen if they need to stop or terminate the EC2 instances?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Your instances are permanently deleted and cannot be recovered.\n- [ ] B. You are still charged for the instances.\n- [ ] C. The instances will automatically restart after a set time.\n- [x] D. You pay only for running instances, not for stopped or terminated ones.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With Amazon EC2, you only pay for running instances, not for ones that are stopped or terminated.\n\n<!-- id: m02-01-introduction-to-amazon-ec2-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nWhat must be specified when preparing to launch an Amazon EC2 instance?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The amount of storage and the number of users\n- [x] B. The type of instance and the operating system\n- [ ] C. The network bandwidth and data transfer limit\n- [ ] D. The instance's location and backup plan\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: You need to the choose EC2 instance type (how powerful you want it) and the Amazon Machine Image (AMI), which determines the operating system and software for your instance.\n","m10-06-auditing-aws-resources-for-compliance.md":"# Module 10: Monitoring, Compliance, and Governance in the AWS Cloud › Auditing AWS Resources for Compliance\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m10-06-auditing-aws-resources-for-compliance-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAn enterprise customer with a large team of developers needs a way to ensure specific configuration guidelines for the developers when creating AWS resources. They want to assess and audit the AWS resources to make sure that the team is using the most cost-effective approved list of Amazon EC2 instances.Which AWS service would best fit the customer's need?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Config\n- [ ] B. AWS Audit Manager\n- [ ] C. AWS Artifact\n- [ ] D. AWS CloudTrail\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Config is the best choice because it will assess, audit, and evaluate the configurations of the developer's AWS resources.\n","m13-02-aws-specialized-services.md":"# Module 13: Well-Architected Solutions › AWS Specialized Services\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m13-02-aws-specialized-services-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA development team for a small marketing company needs a debugging and performance analysis tool to visualize their online application’s behavior. The application is hosted on AWS.Which AWS service should this team choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS X-Ray\n- [ ] B. AWS CodePipeline\n- [ ] C. AWS Amplify\n- [ ] D. AWS AppSync\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: X-Ray provides visualization tools specifically designed for debugging and performance analysis of applications.\n\n<!-- id: m13-02-aws-specialized-services-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA large automotive company wants to use the power of AI in its customer service center. They need a solution that includes call routing, recording, and analytics.Which AWS service can provide these capabilities?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon Connect\n- [ ] B. Amazon WorkSpaces\n- [ ] C. AWS Amplify\n- [ ] D. Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Connect is an AI-powered contact center solution that offers call routing, recording, and analytics capabilities.\n\n<!-- id: m13-02-aws-specialized-services-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nAn IT department needs to provide employees access to several software-as-a-service (SaaS) online applications.Which AWS service can provide this access?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS AppSync\n- [ ] B. AWS IoT Core\n- [x] C. Amazon AppStream 2.0\n- [ ] D. Amazon Connect\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AppStream 2.0 delivers desktop applications to users through web browsers, enabling secure SaaS application access for employees.\n\n<!-- id: m13-02-aws-specialized-services-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nWhich options are Internet of Things (IoT) solutions? (Select TWO.)\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [ ] A. A mobile app to order food from a favorite restaurant\n- [x] B. A wearable device that tracks steps per day on a smartphone\n- [ ] C. A smart TV that recommends shows based on viewing history\n- [x] D. A Wi-Fi enabled plug that can be used to turn off lights remotely\n- [ ] E. An online banking application used to check account balances\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The wearable device that tracks steps on a smartphone and the Wi-Fi enabled plug that can be used to turn off lights remotely are both examples of IoT solutions. Although these other options are digital solutions, they do not involve physical devices that communicate with networked applications.\n","m08-06-introduction-to-data-analytics.md":"# Module 8: AI/ML and Data Analytics › Introduction to Data Analytics\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m08-06-introduction-to-data-analytics-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nData pipelines are automated assembly lines used to make the ETL process efficient and repeatable. What does ETL stand for?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Extract, transform, load\n- [ ] B. Export, translate, link\n- [ ] C. Evaluate, test, launch\n- [ ] D. Explore, transfer, log\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: In data analytics, ETL stands for extract, transform, load. Sometimes, an ELT process is followed in which the transform step is last.\n\n<!-- id: m08-06-introduction-to-data-analytics-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nIn the field of data analytics, analysts transform raw historical data into something useful. What are these analysts working to uncover with this transformed data?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Valuable insights and trends\n- [ ] B. Hardware malfunctions\n- [ ] C. Programming errors and bugs\n- [ ] D. Personal customer information\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: In the field of data analytics, analysts transform raw historical data into valuable insights and trends.\n","m10-03-amazon-cloudwatch.md":"# Module 10: Monitoring, Compliance, and Governance in the AWS Cloud › Amazon CloudWatch\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m10-03-amazon-cloudwatch-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAn ecommerce company is hosting their customer application on multiple Amazon EC2 instances. The application experiences fluctuating traffic and occasional performance issues that are impacting the customer experience.How can Amazon CloudWatch help the customer? (Select THREE.)\n\n_Choose 3_\n\n- [ ] A. CloudWatch can deliver content to the edge locations, closer to where customers are located, to reduce latency.\n- [x] B. CloudWatch dashboards can be customized to visualize the metrics, alarms, and data in a consolidated view.\n- [ ] C. CloudWatch can predict the items that customers will purchase and place those in the ecommerce application shopping cart in the buy again category.\n- [x] D. CloudWatch alarms can be set up to alert when the Amazon EC2 utilization is too high for an extended period and automate more EC2 instances being created to share the load.\n- [x] E. CloudWatch logs can collect data on the EC2 instances and application logs. The logs can gain insights on performance issues or application errors.\n- [ ] F. CloudWatch can design architectures and create all the resources to minimize performance issues.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Client VPN enables you to securely connect users to AWS or on-premises networks. So it would not be the best solution. Also it would not provide the bandwidth needed. Rationale: AWS Site-to-Site private resources would connect the datacenter to the cloud, but it's not the best choice as it would not provide the massive bandwidth needed. Rationale: Direct Connect would provide the bandwidth requirements for the migration as well as the ongoing data transfers in their hybrid solution.\n","m09-02-preventing-unauthorized-access.md":"# Module 9: Security › Preventing Unauthorized Access\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m09-02-preventing-unauthorized-access-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAn administrator who creates an AWS account is provided with the root user credentials. To secure this highly privileged account, they should immediately set a strong password and enable multi-factor authentication (MFA). What does MFA require users to do?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Use a virtual private network (VPN) whenever logging in.\n- [ ] B. Have a credit card on file for identity verification.\n- [ ] C. Change the password every 30 days.\n- [x] D. Provide two or more verification methods to gain access.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: MFA adds an additional layer of security by requiring a password, username, something only the user has on them, such as a physical token. For example, a smartphone app generating a one-time code.\n\n<!-- id: m09-02-preventing-unauthorized-access-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) provides users, groups, roles, and policies so you can configure access based on your company’s specific operational and security needs. Which of these is specifically designed to provide temporary access to permissions?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. IAM groups\n- [x] B. IAM roles\n- [ ] C. IAM policies\n- [ ] D. IAM users\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: An IAM role is an identity someone can assume to gain temporary access to permissions. When someone assumes an IAM role, they abandon all previous permissions they had under a previous role and assume the permissions of the new role.\n\n<!-- id: m09-02-preventing-unauthorized-access-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA financial services company wants to give its accountants access to a particular Amazon S3 bucket. Which of these IAM controls is used to define this access?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. IAM role\n- [x] B. IAM policy\n- [ ] C. IAM user\n- [ ] D. IAM group\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: An IAM policy is a JSON document that allows or denies permission to access AWS services and resources. It can be added to IAM users, groups, and roles to define access to the particular S3 bucket.\n\n<!-- id: m09-02-preventing-unauthorized-access-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA software development team needs to centrally manage its database credentials and API keys on AWS. Which of these services should the team choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS IAM Identity Center\n- [ ] B. AWS Systems Manager\n- [x] C. AWS Secrets Manager\n- [ ] D. AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Secrets Manager can provide the team with a secure way to manage, rotate, and retrieve database credentials, API keys, and other secrets throughout their lifecycle.\n","m10-11-assessment.md":"# Module 10: Monitoring, Compliance, and Governance in the AWS Cloud › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA sportswear company is hosting their application on Amazon EC2 instances. They want to collect metrics on their EC2 instances and they would like notifications when utilization passes thresholds. They also want to have an action configured to automate scaling up the number of EC2 instances when utilization surpasses their threshold.Which AWS service would best meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS CloudTrail\n- [x] B. Amazon CloudWatch\n- [ ] C. AWS Artifact\n- [ ] D. AWS Trusted Advisor\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: CloudWatch can collect the metrics on the EC2 instances, provide insights using dashboards, set alarms on thresholds, and automate the additional EC2 instances.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhich AWS service provides a no-cost, on-demand access to AWS security and compliance reports and select online agreements?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS CloudTrail\n- [x] B. AWS Artifact\n- [ ] C. AWS Trusted Advisor\n- [ ] D. Amazon CloudWatch\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Artifact is a self-service portal that provides on-demand access to AWS security and compliance documentation, including reports.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA financial company with a hybrid cloud solution wants to track changes made to their AWS resources both in the cloud and on premises. Specifically, they want to know who did what, and when.Which AWS service would best meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS CloudTrail\n- [ ] B. AWS Artifact\n- [ ] C. AWS Trusted Advisor\n- [ ] D. Amazon CloudWatch\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: CloudTrail is an AWS service that uses APIs to track who did what, when the action occurred, and on which AWS services and resources.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nAn enterprise customer has grown rapidly and is struggling to manage billing of their AWS resources and accounts. Every employee has created independent accounts with no centralized management or hierarchical groupings of accounts. The customer wants to roll up billing and centralize management into organizational units. Which AWS service would best meet this customer's need?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Trusted Advisor\n- [x] B. AWS Organizations\n- [ ] C. An Availability Zone (AZ)\n- [ ] D. AWS Service Catalog\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With Organizations, you can centrally manage your environment as you scale your AWS resources. It can be used to centralize management, consolidate billing, and implement hierarchical groupings of accounts.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nWhich AWS service provides continuous evaluation and checks of your AWS resources, and provides suggestions to optimize costs, performance, security, and resilience?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS CloudTrail\n- [ ] B. AWS Artifact\n- [ ] C. Amazon CloudWatch\n- [x] D. AWS Trusted Advisor\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Trusted Advisor helps you optimize costs, increase performance, improve security and resilience, and operate at scale in the cloud.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nA financial company is looking for a solution to govern a curated set of AWS resources for their employees. When the employees need to select and start up a new AWS resource, they want to provide a self-service way to create, share, and deploy the AWS resources.Which AWS service would best meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Service Catalog\n- [ ] B. AWS License Manager\n- [ ] C. AWS Artifact\n- [ ] D. AWS Health\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With Service Catalog, you can create, share, and organize from a curated catalog of AWS resources. You can deploy baseline networking resources and security tools for new AWS accounts so that you can govern consistently.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nWhere can customers go to find resources on AWS compliance—for example, information on customer compliance stories, answers to key compliance questions, and an auditing security checklist?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Artifact\n- [ ] B. AWS Management Console\n- [x] C. Customer Compliance Center\n- [ ] D. AWS Organizaitons\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The Customer Compliance Center provides resources to help you learn more about AWS compliance. You can read customer compliance stories to discover how companies in regulated industries have solved various compliance, governance, and audit challenges.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nWhat is the purpose of an AWS Control Tower landing zone?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. It is the enterprise-wide container that holds all your organizational units (OUs), accounts, users, and resources that you want to regulate for compliance.\n- [ ] B. It filters inbound and outbound traffic to Amazon EC2 instances in a virtual private cloud (VPC).\n- [ ] C. It is a logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define.\n- [ ] D. It is a subsection of a virtual private cloud (VPC) where you can isolate resources and control access.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A landing zone is a well-architected multi-account environment that is based on security and compliance best practices. It is the container where you hold all the resources that you want to regulate for compliance.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q9 -->\n## Question 9\n\nA research customer with a large team of developers needs a way to ensure specific configuration guidelines for the developers when creating AWS resources. They want a way to assess and audit the AWS resources to ensure that the team is using the most cost-effective approved list of compute resources.Which solution or feature would meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Audit Manager\n- [ ] B. AWS CloudTrail\n- [ ] C. AWS Artifact\n- [x] D. AWS Config\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Config is the best choice because it will assess, audit, and evaluate the configurations of the developer's AWS resources.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q10 -->\n## Question 10\n\nA customer is using AWS Organizations to centrally manage their company's accounts for billing to optimize and organize costs. They want to set up rules or restrictions on the AWS services, resources, and individual API actions that the users can access.Which feature would meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. A service control policy (SCP)\n- [ ] B. An AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) user\n- [ ] C. A root account\n- [ ] D. An organizational unit (OU)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: An SCP is a policy that lets you place restrictions on the AWS services, resources, and individual API actions that users and roles in each account can access. SCPs can be applied to either OUs or individual member accounts.\n\n<!-- id: m10-11-assessment-q11 -->\n## Question 11\n\nA customer is moving from on premises to the cloud and has decided to use the Bring Your Own License model (BYOL) approach for cost savings. They are concerned about managing the licenses, want a way to reduce the risk of noncompliance, and want to enforce license usage limits.Which solution would best meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS License Manager\n- [ ] B. AWS Service Catalog\n- [ ] C. AWS Control Tower\n- [ ] D. AWS Organizations\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: License Manager helps reduce the risk of noncompliance by enforcing license usage limits, blocking new launches, and using other controls.\n","m12-02-aws-cloud-adoption-framework.md":"# Module 12: Migrating to the AWS Cloud › AWS Cloud Adoption Framework\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m12-02-aws-cloud-adoption-framework-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhich perspective of the AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF) includes principles and patterns for implementing new solutions in the cloud and migrating on-premises workloads to the new platform in the cloud? It uses a variety of architectural models to understand and communicate the structure of IT systems.\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Operations perspective\n- [ ] B. People perspective\n- [ ] C. Business perspective\n- [x] D. Platform perspective\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A virtual private gateway with a VPN connection would work. And using a private subnet is exactly what they need!\n","m11-05-aws-marketplace-and-aws-partners.md":"# Module 11: Pricing and Support › AWS Marketplace and AWS Partners\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m11-05-aws-marketplace-and-aws-partners-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou are a new cloud solutions architect at a growing tech company. Your manager has asked you to explore the AWS Marketplace to find solutions that can help improve your company's operational efficiency and reduce costs. Based on what you've learned, which options are available on the AWS Marketplace?\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [x] A. Software as a service (SaaS) applications\n- [ ] B. Cloud storage\n- [ ] C. Virtual machines (VMs)\n- [x] D. Datasets and analytics tools\n- [ ] E. Hardware products for on-premises deployment\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The AWS Marketplace offers a wide range of SaaS applications that the company can subscribe to and use directly within their AWS environment. It also provides various datasets and analytics tools that can help gain insights and make data-driven decisions.\n"};
